{
  "raw": {
    "https://careers.kenyon.edu/jobs/marilyn-yarbrough-dissertation-teaching-fellowship-gambier-oh-ohio-united-states-33dabe45-dcf2-4538-9f96-19c8cb971abd": {
      "title": "Marilyn Yarbrough Dissertation/Teaching Fellowship",
      "description": "Marilyn Yarbrough Dissertation/Teaching Fellowship - Gambier, OH, Ohio, United States Marilyn Yarbrough Dissertation/Teaching Fellowship - Gambier, OH, Ohio, United States Kiosk mode Job Opportunities Marilyn Yarbrough Dissertation/Teaching Fellowship 493377 Gambier, OH, Ohio Provost Faculty Add to favorites View favorites Marilyn Yarbrough Dissertation/Teaching Fellowship This award is named in honor of the late Marilyn Yarbrough, Kenyon parent and trustee. A legal scholar and university administrator who was a former editor of the Black Law Journal and a member of the Pulitzer Prize Board, Marilyn Yarbrough often addressed gender and racial discrimination in her scholarship and teaching. Download a list of previous Marilyn Yarbrough Teaching Fellows. One of the most significant challenges confronting small liberal arts colleges in the United States today is ensuring that the faculty is representative of the population of the United States in all its dimensions. Such a faculty benefits students, faculty, and staff alike by enriching the nature of the educational experience for all. We recognize, though, that many young scholars frequently choose to pursue their careers as teachers and scholars at research universities rather than at small liberal arts colleges. In order to encourage such scholars to consider college rather than university teaching, Kenyon College offers the Marilyn Yarbrough Dissertation/Teaching Fellowship. The program is for scholars in the final stages of their doctoral work who need only to finish the dissertation to complete requirements for the Ph.D. We hope the experience of living and working for a year at Kenyon will encourage these fellows to consider a liberal arts college as a place to begin their careers as teachers and scholars. In the past, fellowships have been awarded in: African and African American studies, American studies, Anthropology, Art History, Asian and Middle East studies, Biology, Classics, English, History, Latine Studies, Math, Modern Languages and Literatures (Spanish), Music, Political Science, Religious Studies, Sociology, Gender and Sexuality Studies. Kenyon will provide a stipend of $42,000 plus health benefits, housing (or equivalent allowance), and a small moving allowance. The College will also provide some allowance to cover research, travel to conferences, and professional expenses. The fellow will be provided an office, a networked computer and administrative support services. The fellow is expected to write the dissertation and to teach one course each semester, usually in the fellow's general research area. Fellows are also expected to offer a college lecture or departmental seminar on the dissertation topic at some point during the academic year in residence. Kenyon College assumes that the fellow will participate in the intellectual life of his/her home department, as well as in the broader cultural life of the College. Our primary expectation, however, and the main focus of this fellowship, is the completion of the dissertation. Eligibility to apply for the Marilyn Yarbrough Dissertation/Teaching Fellowship is limited to those meeting all of the following four criteria who are citizens or nationals of the United States or otherwise \"protected individuals\" as defined in 8 USC 1324b(a)(3)(B). Members of groups underrepresented in their fields (whatever their backgrounds), including men in fields that attract mostly women, or women in fields that attract mostly men; and persons who are first-generation college attendees. Individuals who are enrolled in a research-based Ph.D. program in one of the following fields: African and African American studies, American studies, anthropology, art, art history, Asian and Middle East studies, biology, biochemistry, chemistry, classics, dance, drama, economics, English, environmental studies, history, humanities, international studies, latine studies, legal studies, mathematics, modern languages and literature, music, neuroscience, philosophy, physics, political science, public policy, psychology, religious studies, scientific computing, sociology, and gender and sexuality studies. Individuals who aspire to a teaching and research career. Persons who have not yet earned a doctoral degree at any time and in any field. Although holders of F-1 visas are not eligible for this fellowship, applicants do not need to be citizens of the United States. The MYDF search will accept applications from mid-October through Dec. 31. To apply, candidates should visit the online application site found at http://careers.kenyon.edu. A complete application will be composed of 1) a cover letter discussing the applicant’s research and scholarship undertaken, its relevance to the field or discipline, prior teaching experience, and the applicant's eligibility for the fellowship; 2) a Curriculum Vitae; and 3) contact information for three professional recommendations (system will automatically email reference writers). All application materials must be submitted electronically through Kenyon's employment website at http://careers.kenyon.edu Compensation and Benefits Salaries at Kenyon are competitive and are commensurate with experience. There are a number of faculty development opportunities (e.g. travel, research funds, etc.) for which appointees are eligible. In addition to an attractive salary, Kenyon offers benefits for employees and their family members. Children of employees are eligible for 100% tuition waivers at Kenyon, and through the Great Lakes Colleges Association , children of employees are eligible for 85% tuition waivers at fifteen other of the nation's finest liberal arts colleges. We also offer health and dental insurance, TIAA retirement, and many other benefits, including provisions for a spouse, families, and domestic partners. Details about benefits as well as conditions of employment are described more fully in our Faculty Handbook . Kenyon is a great place to live and work. To discover why it should be your next home, click here . Kenyon College is an equal opportunity employer, and we welcome applications from all qualified individuals. It is the College's policy to evaluate qualified applicants without regard to race, color, national origin, ancestry, sex, gender, gender identity, gender expression, sexual orientation, physical and/or mental disability, age, religion, medical condition, veteran status, marital status, or any other characteristic protected by institutional policy or state, local, or federal law. Kenyon College has a strong commitment to an inclusive environment that welcomes all voices and perspectives. Back to job search Apply Now First Name (required) d2fcef91 Last Name (required) 327eae3c Email (required) a1c56b0c Refer someone to this job Apply Please wait... Done Not You? Thank you Recommended Jobs Assistant Professor of Political Science, tenure-track Gambier, OH, Ohio Political Science The Department of Political Science at Kenyon College invites applications for a tenure-track position in Modern Political Theory. We seek an individual broadly trained in the history of political philosophy who would teach introductory and intermediate courses in political theory (Quest for Justice, Modern Quest), as well as advanced courses in their areas of specialty. Successful candidates will demonstrate a commitment to the liberal arts, strong teaching, deep understanding of the history surrounding political thought, and scholarly promise. To apply, please visit careers.kenyon.edu. Executive Assistant for The Kenyon Review Gambier, OH, Ohio Kenyon Review The Executive Assistant plays a central role in supporting the organization's leadership and ensuring smooth day-to-day operations by providing including grant coordination, gift acknowledgement, board administration, and conference/event logistics. The ideal candidate is highly organized, proactive, and passionate about supporting the literary arts. Assistant Professor of Political Science & Environmental Studies Gambier, OH, Ohio Political Science The Political Science Department and Environmental Studies Department at Kenyon College invite applications for a tenure-track position beginning July 1, 2027. Qualified applicants will have a strong teaching and research background in comparative politics, environmental politics, and international relations. The successful candidate would be appointed in both Political Science (60%) and Environmental Studies (40%), teach established courses in the curricula of both departments, and contribute upper-level courses on environmental politics and policy in their areas of expertise. We will prioritize candidates with a strong record of teaching and research; a commitment to student advising and mentorship; and plans to incorporate student researchers into their research. All application materials must be submitted electronically to http://careers.kenyon.edu. A complete application will include: 1) a cover letter discussing the applicant’s teaching experience, research interests and scholarship; 2) a curriculum vitae; 3) a statement of teaching philosophy with evidence of teaching excellence and a discussion of courses that the candidate has taught and can teach; 4) a writing sample; 5) an unofficial graduate transcript; and 6) contact information for three references. Review of completed applications will begin immediately and will continue until the position is filled. To ensure full consideration, please submit all application materials by September 15, 2026. Additional materials may be requested from candidates at a later date. Sign up for job alerts First Name (required) 46918b7d Last Name (required) 27ab8ed9 Email (required) 2ae2beff Job Alert 4079d4e7 Finalize your job alert by selecting criteria from the dropdowns below. You can select multiple options from each dropdown by returning to the combobox and re-entering the list of options. Submit at the end to create your job alert. Departments Provost Provost Employment Type Faculty Faculty Locations Gambier, OH, Ohio, United States Gambier, OH, Ohio, United States Send Please wait... Done Not You? Thank you Candidate Details We use cookies Some are necessary to operate the website and its functions. Others help personalise, improve content and services to show you the most relevant job opportunities. With the decision \"Accept essential only\" we will respect your privacy and will not set cookies that aren't necessary for the operation of the site. Accept essential only Accept all Please choose the location(s)"
    },
    "https://careers.kenyon.edu/jobs/facilities-services-supervisor-gambier-oh-ohio-united-states": {
      "title": "Facilities Services Supervisor",
      "description": "Facilities Services Supervisor - Gambier, OH, Ohio, United States Facilities Services Supervisor - Gambier, OH, Ohio, United States Kiosk mode Job Opportunities Facilities Services Supervisor 493375 Gambier, OH, Ohio Maintenance Exempt Staff Add to favorites View favorites Kenyon College is conducting a search for a qualified candidate to fill the position of Facilities Services Supervisor in the Maintenance Department. The Facilities Services Supervisor reports to the Director of Facility Operations. The Facilities Services Supervisor is a full-time position responsible for the supervision of the Facilities Rover team and Storeroom/Receiving clerks. The Facilities Services Supervisor fills a critical role as a liaison to the Kenyon Events Office and other campus partners for the coordination and setup of events throughout campus. Primary responsibilities for this position include managing: Rover Staff: By work order request, set up for events around the campus. By work order request, move/remove/deliver furniture and equipment to work spaces about the campus. Maintain rover equipment and set up furniture. Maintain Campus furniture and equipment storage facility. Special Events: Participate in team planning of events. Directly responsible for final set-up of all special events to include: Trustee meetings, Alumni events, Admission events, Athletic events (not game set up), Artist Series, Concert Board Activities, Convocation, Commencement, Student Celebrations, and other Unique Special Events. Work closely with the Office of Event Management to help improve the request system. Coordinate directly with the specific Event coordinator to ensure accuracy of information. Coordinate directly with outside companies supplying equipment and furnishings. Trash/Recycling: Develop, maintain and coordinate all activities for the Kenyon recycling program. Review all equipment utilized by the rovers, recycling team members, and refuse truck drivers. Manage trash pick-up and removal from all campus buildings. Coordinate with office of Green Initiatives with regard to Campus Recycle Initiatives, equipment purchases and Student group projects. Maintain records of total recycle collection by fiscal year, by commodity compared to total Recycle/Trash collection. Other Job Duties: Utilize a work order system to distribute work, maintain staff productivity, and coordinate with other teams. Supervise storage, allocation, distribution, set-up and maintenance of all special events equipment including: tents, canopies, chairs, tables, staging, flags, lecterns, podiums, risers, and any other special events equipment. Develop and monitor a preventative maintenance program for all equipment utilized by team members. Coordinate outside contractors/vendors work: Develop scope for work to be completed. Schedule work to coincide or cause minimal disruption to college operations. Follow-up on all work for quality, workmanship, and timeliness, reporting any deficiencies. Maintain personnel records: Track vacation requests and time-off requests. Monitor the staff’s regular hours, overtime hours opportunities, and schedules. Review and approve daily time sheets of direct reports. We invite all interested applicants to apply. We understand that not everyone will have all of the listed qualifications. We are an institution committed to helping our employees to develop the necessary skills to be successful in their position, which includes training, professional development, or other education opportunities and experiences. Applicants are encouraged to communicate how their education, work, and experiences may be transferable to this role in ways that may not be obvious. Qualifications: Supervisory experience in an academic campus. Valid Ohio Driver License. Ability to work in conditions inside and outside that are considered temperature extremes. Requires physical exertion to manually move, lift, carry, pull, and push heavy objects or materials up to 50 pounds. Knowledge, Skills, Abilities: Excellent organizational, interpersonal, and writing skills. Outstanding customer service skills is a must. Project Management experience. Software proficiencies: Microsoft Office, Google Suite, CMMS applications. Anticipated Start Date: 15 November 2026. Kenyon College is a nationally prominent, private liberal arts college where academic excellence goes hand in hand with a strong sense of community and close relationships among students and professors. Compensation and Benefits Salaries at Kenyon are competitive and commensurate with experience. In addition to an attractive salary, Kenyon offers benefits for employees and their family members. Children of employees are eligible for 100% tuition waivers at Kenyon, and through the Great Lakes Colleges Association , children of employees are eligible for 90% tuition waivers at twenty-three other of the nation's finest liberal arts colleges. We also offer health, dental and vision insurance, TIAA retirement, and many other benefits , including provisions for a spouse, families, and domestic partners. Details about benefits as well as conditions of employment are described more fully in our Staff Handbook . Kenyon is a unique place to live and work. To discover why it should be your next home, click here . Kenyon College is an equal opportunity employer, and we welcome applications from all qualified individuals. It is the College's policy to evaluate qualified applicants without regard to race, color, national origin, ancestry, sex, gender, gender identity, gender expression, sexual orientation, physical and/or mental disability, age, religion, medical condition, veteran status, marital status, or any other characteristic protected by institutional policy or state, local, or federal law. Kenyon College has a strong commitment to an inclusive environment that welcomes all voices and perspectives. Back to job search Apply Now First Name (required) 6432bf5b Last Name (required) 57f61b8c Email (required) d8730096 Refer someone to this job Apply Please wait... Done Not You? Thank you Recommended Jobs Custodian, Third Shift Gambier, OH, Ohio Maintenance Kenyon College is conducting a search for a qualified applicant to fill the position of Custodian, Third Shift. Maintaining college buildings and facilities, keeping them free of hazard and presenting a neat, clean appearance. Must have the ability to work independently and as a member of a team. The hourly rate of pay for this full-time with benefits position is $25.70/hour and includes a 7% shift differential. Work days are Monday-Friday, 10:00 p.m. to 6:30 a.m., with a 30-minute unpaid lunch. Engagement Events Program Coordinator Gambier, OH, Ohio Alumni and Parent Engagement Kenyon College is searching for an Engagement Events Program Coordinator. Reporting to the Sr. Associate Director of Alumni and Parent Engagement Events, and will work closely with the Director of Alumni Engagement. The role will provide support for alumni, parent, and donor events sponsored by the Advancement Division and support to our campus partners as needed. Senior Facilities Planner/Project Manager Gambier, OH, Ohio Campus Operations Kenyon College is conducting a search for a qualified candidate to fill the position of Senior Facilities Planner/Project Manager. Reporting to the Chief Operating Officer (COO), the Senior Facilities Planner/Project Manager is responsible for the management of planning and design initiatives and the execution of capital projects – including new construction, renewal, and renovation. The position will be responsible for developing project scopes and budgets, supervision of design teams, general contractors, and construction management firms, and overseeing contracts and budgets. The position will support the COO in developing specific planning initiatives and long-range facilities plans and capital budgets. Sign up for job alerts First Name (required) 92642645 Last Name (required) 73ea9672 Email (required) 40378814 Job Alert 3951f8e6 Finalize your job alert by selecting criteria from the dropdowns below. You can select multiple options from each dropdown by returning to the combobox and re-entering the list of options. Submit at the end to create your job alert. Departments Maintenance Maintenance Employment Type Exempt Staff Exempt Staff Locations Gambier, OH, Ohio, United States Gambier, OH, Ohio, United States Send Please wait... Done Not You? Thank you Candidate Details We use cookies Some are necessary to operate the website and its functions. Others help personalise, improve content and services to show you the most relevant job opportunities. With the decision \"Accept essential only\" we will respect your privacy and will not set cookies that aren't necessary for the operation of the site. Accept essential only Accept all Please choose the location(s)"
