    "https://careers.kenyon.edu/jobs/engagement-events-program-coordinator-gambier-oh-ohio-united-states": {
      "title": "Engagement Events Program Coordinator",
      "description": "Engagement Events Program Coordinator - Gambier, OH, Ohio, United States Engagement Events Program Coordinator - Gambier, OH, Ohio, United States Kiosk mode Job Opportunities Engagement Events Program Coordinator 493374 Gambier, OH, Ohio Alumni and Parent Engagement Exempt Staff Add to favorites View favorites Kenyon College is conducting a search for a qualified candidate to fill the position of Engagement Events Program Coordinator. Reporting to the Sr. Associate Director of Alumni and Parent Engagement Events, and working closely with the Director of Alumni Engagement, the coordinator is responsible for providing support for events involving alumni, parents and donors that are sponsored by the Advancement Division as well as providing occasional collaborative support to our campus partners. These events include but are not limited to: volunteer meetings, virtual events, Homecoming Weekend, Family Weekend, and Reunion Weekend. Essential Functions Manage the College’s online event registration system for events of varying size and complexity, often with multiple registrations open simultaneously. Respond to all alumni inquiries—via email and phone—regarding event registration, including providing clear guidance, troubleshooting issues, and offering step-by-step support when needed. Organize and complete all housing assignments for alumni during reunion weekend. Provide logistical support for events, including arranging accommodations, catering, transportation, venue reservations, permits, and special requests as needed. Coordinate event materials such as nametags, parking permits, and signage. Track and report on event attendance, payments, and expenditures; support post-event surveys and communications. Maintain and update event-related content on the Office of Alumni and Parent Engagement web pages. Manage the Kenyon Events App, ensuring event information is accurate and accessible. Provide technical support for virtual events and online programs. Other Functions Respond to general inquiries by phone and email from alumni, parents, students, and campus or external partners. Support and steward alumni and parent communities, including donors. Oversee inventory of event and registration supplies. Provide on-campus event support for the Director of Donor Engagement, as needed. Assist with off-campus programs, regional events, and other office initiatives as required. Participate in search committees and cross-campus collaborations as requested. Knowledge, Skills, Abilities, and Success Factors The ability to multitask, plan ahead, organize and manage numerous event details simultaneously is paramount. Candidate must possess a professional and friendly demeanor, and remain poised under pressure. Must be flexible and able to react calmly, quickly and efficiently to any issues that arise. Ability to develop new methods, adapt to the changing needs of the office and establish appropriate procedures. Ability to work independently as well as part of a team. Ability to make sound decisions under pressure and the ability to be creative when problem solving. Supervisory Responsibilities Supervisory responsibilities include student workers, temporary student workers and student interns. The staff member also serves as the lead at the Registration Center, providing guidance, support, and direction to Registration Center staff during events. Working Conditions Work is generally performed in an office environment and requires the ability to operate standard office equipment as well as the ability to sit for long periods of time. The ability to lift items weighing 30 pounds or less and move tables and chairs when necessary for events is required. Hybrid work environment opportunities with the option to work remotely for part of the week during most of the calendar year. Attendance at marquee College events hosted by Advancement which may include some weekends and evenings. Minimum Qualifications Two year college degree or three years’ experience in planning and organizing large events or projects. Strong computer skills are required, including Microsoft Office programs and familiarity with Google office suite, data management, mobile payment, online content management and reservation systems, as well as a willingness to learn new systems. Ability to do long- and short-range planning. Must be accurate and timely. Willingness to work occasional weekends and evenings. Please note that the following weekends will be required; Homecoming Weekend (mid-late September), Family Weekend (early-mid October) and Reunion Weekend (May including Memorial Day Weekend). The ability to obtain College driver certification is desirable. Kenyon College is a nationally prominent, private liberal arts college where academic excellence goes hand in hand with a strong sense of community and close relationships among students and professors. Compensation and Benefits Salaries at Kenyon are competitive and commensurate with experience. In addition to an attractive salary, Kenyon offers benefits for employees and their family members. Children of employees are eligible for 100% tuition waivers at Kenyon, and through the Great Lakes Colleges Association , children of employees are eligible for 90% tuition waivers at twenty-three other of the nation's finest liberal arts colleges. We also offer health, dental and vision insurance, TIAA retirement, and many other benefits , including provisions for a spouse, families, and domestic partners. Details about benefits as well as conditions of employment are described more fully in our Staff Handbook. Kenyon is a unique place to live and work. To discover why it should be your next home, click here . Kenyon College is an equal opportunity employer, and we welcome applications from all qualified individuals. It is the College's policy to evaluate qualified applicants without regard to race, color, national origin, ancestry, sex, gender, gender identity, gender expression, sexual orientation, physical and/or mental disability, age, religion, medical condition, veteran status, marital status, or any other characteristic protected by institutional policy or state, local, or federal law. Kenyon College has a strong commitment to an inclusive environment that welcomes all voices and perspectives. Back to job search Apply Now First Name (required) 9a703560 Last Name (required) e7d0e4db Email (required) b52df4b8 Refer someone to this job Apply Please wait... Done Not You? Thank you Recommended Jobs There are currently no jobs matching this criteria Sign up for job alerts First Name (required) c99e86b6 Last Name (required) 26d87079 Email (required) e0dea9f2 Job Alert df9dd7c8 Finalize your job alert by selecting criteria from the dropdowns below. You can select multiple options from each dropdown by returning to the combobox and re-entering the list of options. Submit at the end to create your job alert. Departments Alumni and Parent Engagement Alumni and Parent Engagement Employment Type Exempt Staff Exempt Staff Locations Gambier, OH, Ohio, United States Gambier, OH, Ohio, United States Send Please wait... Done Not You? Thank you Candidate Details We use cookies Some are necessary to operate the website and its functions. Others help personalise, improve content and services to show you the most relevant job opportunities. With the decision \"Accept essential only\" we will respect your privacy and will not set cookies that aren't necessary for the operation of the site. Accept essential only Accept all Please choose the location(s)"
    },
    "https://careers.kenyon.edu/jobs/digital-stewardship-librarian-gambier-oh-ohio-united-states": {
      "title": "Digital Stewardship Librarian",
      "description": "Digital Stewardship Librarian - Gambier, OH, Ohio, United States Digital Stewardship Librarian - Gambier, OH, Ohio, United States Kiosk mode Job Opportunities Digital Stewardship Librarian 493373 Gambier, OH, Ohio Library Services Exempt Staff Add to favorites View favorites Kenyon College is conducting a search for a qualified candidate to fill the position of Digital Stewardship Librarian. This 12 month, full time, position is primarily on campus with some remote flexibility. Help Kenyon's digital collections last Kenyon's digital collections, from digitized treasures to born-digital records, need someone to make sure they're findable, usable, and preserved. As our Digital Stewardship Librarian, you'll be that person: the expert who shapes how we describe, protect, and share our collections, and who helps the campus community get the most from them. You'll join the Special Collections and Archives Department, report to the Director, and work with library colleagues and partners across the college. If you're a recent graduate with a degree in digital librarianship or something similar, this is a great place to make your mark. What you'll do Keep our digital collections safe and sustainable Prepare digitized and born-digital materials for ingest, stabilization, and storage, following best practices and archival standards Serve as the primary administrator of Kenyon's repository platform, Digital Kenyon (Digital Commons), and related preservation tools, building the processes to describe, ingest, publish, manage, migrate, and preserve our digital objects Be the go-to expert on preservation systems, digitization workflows, and lifecycle management, and advise on the policies that guide them Shape our digital strategy and bring projects to life Grow and manage the tools and services that keep our digital collections scalable, and define requirements for the digital assets we create or acquire Partner with faculty and campus stakeholders on grants, research, and course-integrated projects Lead digital projects from plan to delivery, translating between technical and non-technical audiences so everyone knows the goals, timelines, and deliverables Teach and consult: train faculty, students, and staff, and help them put digital tools to work Explore new preservation and institutional repository platforms with your colleagues, and migrate content between systems when the time comes Connect with students and faculty Serve as liaison to academic programs, potentially in data, computing, and math connected disciplines Teach in courses, hold research consultations, and develop discipline-specific resources Work with faculty and students on information, digital, and AI literacy Grow with the profession Represent Kenyon in the OhioLINK and The Five Colleges of Ohio consortia Attend conferences, workshops, and seminars to keep learning Track usage of digital resources, share best practices with colleagues, and recommend purchases to library leadership What you bring Required An ALA-accredited master's degree in library science or equivalent, completed by June 2027, or a related degree plus library experience Education or experience in digital collections, digitization, born-digital archives, digital preservation, metadata, or related work in a library, archive, museum, cultural heritage organization, or similar setting We'll be especially excited about Hands-on experience with digital collections or repositories, especially using Digital Commons Knowledge of current metadata schemes and standards Strong communication and organizational skills, including clear documentation processes Familiarity with trends in digital libraries, digitization standards, preservation, and rights management Comfort working independently and as part of a team A knack for learning new technologies quickly and teaching them to others, whatever their technical background How to apply Interested in joining us? Apply through the Kenyon employment system with a cover letter, resume, and references. In your letter, we'd love to hear what draws you to this role, how your experience fits, and how you'd contribute to Kenyon's mission, along with your perspective on diversity, equity, inclusion, and accessibility. Applications are due by November 9, 2026. $58,000–$64,000 per year, commensurate with experience and qualifications. About Kenyon Kenyon College is a nationally prominent, private liberal arts college where academic excellence goes hand in hand with a strong sense of community and close relationships among students and professors. Compensation and Benefits Salaries at Kenyon are competitive and commensurate with experience. In addition to an attractive salary, Kenyon offers benefits for employees and their family members. Children of employees are eligible for 100% tuition waivers at Kenyon, and through the Great Lakes Colleges Association , children of employees are eligible for 90% tuition waivers at twenty-three other of the nation's finest liberal arts colleges. We also offer health, dental and vision insurance, TIAA retirement, and many other benefits , including provisions for a spouse, families, and domestic partners. Details about benefits as well as conditions of employment are described more fully in our Staff Handbook . Kenyon is a unique place to live and work. To discover why it should be your next home, click here . Kenyon College is an equal opportunity employer, and we welcome applications from all qualified individuals. It is the College's policy to evaluate qualified applicants without regard to race, color, national origin, ancestry, sex, gender, gender identity, gender expression, sexual orientation, physical and/or mental disability, age, religion, medical condition, veteran status, marital status, or any other characteristic protected by institutional policy or state, local, or federal law. Kenyon College has a strong commitment to an inclusive environment that welcomes all voices and perspectives. Back to job search Apply Now First Name (required) d4531b6f Last Name (required) e3196c0a Email (required) da845d4d Refer someone to this job Apply Please wait... Done Not You? Thank you Recommended Jobs Assistant Director of Alumni and Parent Engagement Gambier, OH, Ohio Alumni and Parent Engagement Kenyon College is conducting a search for a qualified candidate to fill the position of Assistant Director of Alumni and Parent Engagement. The Assistant Director of Alumni and Parent Engagement (APE) is part of a team within the Advancement division. The Office of APE oversees events, programs and outreach designed to increase and support meaningful engagement for Kenyon’s alumni and parent communities. The candidate will embrace innovation and strategic decision-making, thrive connecting with alumni virtually and in person, and work in a hybrid work environment. Executive Assistant for The Kenyon Review Gambier, OH, Ohio Kenyon Review The Executive Assistant plays a central role in supporting the organization's leadership and ensuring smooth day-to-day operations by providing including grant coordination, gift acknowledgement, board administration, and conference/event logistics. The ideal candidate is highly organized, proactive, and passionate about supporting the literary arts. Engagement Events Program Coordinator Gambier, OH, Ohio Alumni and Parent Engagement Kenyon College is searching for an Engagement Events Program Coordinator. Reporting to the Sr. Associate Director of Alumni and Parent Engagement Events, and will work closely with the Director of Alumni Engagement. The role will provide support for alumni, parent, and donor events sponsored by the Advancement Division and support to our campus partners as needed. Sign up for job alerts First Name (required) dffb32d8 Last Name (required) 874de1c5 Email (required) 8120fe55 Job Alert ded1675d Finalize your job alert by selecting criteria from the dropdowns below. You can select multiple options from each dropdown by returning to the combobox and re-entering the list of options. Submit at the end to create your job alert. Departments Library Services Library Services Employment Type Exempt Staff Exempt Staff Locations Gambier, OH, Ohio, United States Gambier, OH, Ohio, United States Send Please wait... Done Not You? Thank you Candidate Details We use cookies Some are necessary to operate the website and its functions. Others help personalise, improve content and services to show you the most relevant job opportunities. With the decision \"Accept essential only\" we will respect your privacy and will not set cookies that aren't necessary for the operation of the site. Accept essential only Accept all Please choose the location(s)"
