    "https://careers.kenyon.edu/jobs/custodian-third-shift-gambier-oh-ohio-united-states-89d255ce-5f10-437a-9dd4-4f1d961bc9da": {
      "title": "Custodian, Third Shift",
      "description": "Custodian, Third Shift - Gambier, OH, Ohio, United States Custodian, Third Shift - Gambier, OH, Ohio, United States Kiosk mode Job Opportunities Custodian, Third Shift 493355 Gambier, OH, Ohio Maintenance Non-Exempt Staff Add to favorites View favorites Kenyon College is conducting a search for a qualified applicant to fill the position of Custodian, Third Shift. Maintaining college buildings and facilities, keeping them free of hazard and presenting a neat, clean appearance. Must have the ability to work independently and as a member of a team. The hourly rate of pay for this full-time with benefits position is $25.70/hour and includes a 7% shift differential. Work days are Monday-Friday, 10:00 p.m. to 6:30 a.m., with a 30-minute unpaid lunch. Principal Duties and Responsibilities: Lift, carry, and move materials, supplies, furniture in a safe and careful manner. Use various hand and/or power cleaning equipment such as: dust and scrub mops, vacuum cleaners, buffer/floor polishers and carpet shampoo/extractor equipment, use of a step ladder and snow removal equipment. Use various chemicals and cleaning products in a safe manner in accordance with manufacturer’s instructions and material safety data sheets. The ability to clean toilet fixtures and showers. Perform various other tasks/duties as assigned by a supervisor. Minimum Qualifications: Ability to use powered cleaning equipment Ability to read, comprehend and follow verbal and/or written instructions for work assignments. Ability to work independently or in a group with minimal supervision. Ability to work at heights on ladders to change bulbs and clean windows. Ability to lift, move and transport materials, supplies and equipment up to 50lbs. Must have a valid driver’s license. Previous custodial experience preferred but not required for the right candidate. Benefits Kenyon offers benefits for employees and their family members. Children of employees are eligible for 100% tuition waivers at Kenyon, and through the Great Lakes Colleges Association , children of employees are eligible for 90% tuition waivers at twenty-three other of the nation's finest liberal arts colleges. We also offer health, dental and vision insurance, TIAA retirement, and many other benefits , including provisions for a spouse, families, and domestic partners. Details about benefits as well as conditions of employment are described more fully in our Staff Handbook . Kenyon is a unique place to live and work. To discover why it should be your next home, click here . Kenyon College is an equal opportunity employer, and we welcome applications from all qualified individuals. It is the College's policy to evaluate qualified applicants without regard to race, color, national origin, ancestry, sex, gender, gender identity, gender expression, sexual orientation, physical and/or mental disability, age, religion, medical condition, veteran status, marital status, or any other characteristic protected by institutional policy or state, local, or federal law. Kenyon College has a strong commitment to an inclusive environment that welcomes all voices and perspectives. Back to job search Apply Now First Name (required) 6d6502b2 Last Name (required) 0d7c4f66 Email (required) b423c110 Refer someone to this job Apply Please wait... Done Not You? Thank you Recommended Jobs Student Accounts Coordinator Gambier, OH, Ohio Accounting Kenyon College is conducting a search for a qualified candidate to serve in the position of Student Accounts Coordinator for the Accounting Office. The hourly rate of pay for this full-time with benefits position is $17.96. Successful completion of duties requires a thorough understanding of, and adherence to, College Policies. Willingness and ability to work collaboratively as well as independently is required. General responsibility includes assistance in the management and maintenance of student account records, billings, receipts, maintenance of department records on Federal Perkins and Institutional student loans. Executive Assistant for The Kenyon Review Gambier, OH, Ohio Kenyon Review The Executive Assistant plays a central role in supporting the organization's leadership and ensuring smooth day-to-day operations by providing including grant coordination, gift acknowledgement, board administration, and conference/event logistics. The ideal candidate is highly organized, proactive, and passionate about supporting the literary arts. Facilities Services Supervisor Gambier, OH, Ohio Maintenance Kenyon College is conducting a search for a qualified candidate to fill the position of Facilities Services Supervisor in the Maintenance Department. The Facilities Services Supervisor reports to the Director of Facility Operations. The Facilities Services Supervisor is a full-time position responsible for the supervision of the Facilities Rover team and Storeroom/Receiving clerks. The Facilities Services Supervisor fills a critical role as a liaison to the Kenyon Events Office and other campus partners for the coordination and setup of events throughout campus. Sign up for job alerts First Name (required) f7876b27 Last Name (required) 95f2ce1b Email (required) bed8bb9d Job Alert bd609b05 Finalize your job alert by selecting criteria from the dropdowns below. You can select multiple options from each dropdown by returning to the combobox and re-entering the list of options. Submit at the end to create your job alert. Departments Maintenance Maintenance Employment Type Non-Exempt Staff Non-Exempt Staff Locations Gambier, OH, Ohio, United States Gambier, OH, Ohio, United States Send Please wait... Done Not You? Thank you Candidate Details We use cookies Some are necessary to operate the website and its functions. Others help personalise, improve content and services to show you the most relevant job opportunities. With the decision \"Accept essential only\" we will respect your privacy and will not set cookies that aren't necessary for the