    "https://careers.kenyon.edu/jobs/director-of-grants-gambier-oh-ohio-united-states": {
      "title": "Director of Grants",
      "description": "Director of Grants - Gambier, OH, Ohio, United States Director of Grants - Gambier, OH, Ohio, United States Kiosk mode Job Opportunities Director of Grants 493370 Gambier, OH, Ohio Provost Exempt Staff Add to favorites View favorites Kenyon College is seeking qualified applicants to fill the position of Director of Grants. Reporting to the Provost, the Director of Grants will provide strategic leadership for continued development of a vibrant, collaborative, and inclusive culture of grant-seeking at Kenyon College. The Director will lead a highly effective, service-oriented office that partners closely with faculty, academic leaders, the Business Office and the Advancement Division to expand opportunities for external support of Kenyon’s research, creative activity, scholarship, pedagogy, and institutional priorities. This is an exciting opportunity for an experienced grants professional to help shape the next chapter of sponsored projects at a leading liberal arts college. The Director will combine strategic vision with hands-on engagement, working directly with faculty to identify funding opportunities, develop competitive proposals, and navigate the full grant life cycle. The Director will also play an important institutional role in identifying and developing opportunities for larger, collaborative grants and external partnerships, working in close collaboration with the Office of the Provost and Advancement. The Director will have the opportunity to envision and shape the future structure and priorities of the grants office. The successful candidate will bring strong knowledge of sponsored research and grant administration, a collaborative and entrepreneurial spirit, excellent communication skills, and a genuine enthusiasm for helping faculty and academic programs thrive. The hiring range for this position is $110,000–$120,000 annually, commensurate with experience and qualifications. This is a 12-month position with an expectation of regular, in-person work on campus, with some flexibility for remote work as needed. Key Responsibilities Lead, manage, and continually improve grant-seeking activities across the full grant life cycle, from idea development and opportunity identification through proposal development, submission, award, and post-award-management. Develop and advance strategies that strengthen a campus-wide culture of grant seeking and increase faculty engagement with external funding opportunities. Meet regularly with faculty members to understand their research, creative, scholarly, and pedagogical agendas and help connect their work with appropriate external funding opportunities. Identify emerging funding trends, institutional opportunities, and areas of strategic alignment that can support Kenyon’s academic priorities. Work with the Office of the Provost to identify opportunities for collaborative and multidisciplinary proposals, faculty development, and institutional capacity building. Lead and develop the grants office by hiring and supervising appropriate support staff. Work closely with the Assistant Controller and other designated staff in the Business Office on grant-related budgetary matters, compliance with Uniform Guidance and sponsor regulations, College policies, submission and award processes, subaward negotiations, and post-award oversight. Serve as one of the College’s three designated Authorized Organizational Representatives (AOR), along with the Assistant Controller and Provost, with responsibility for institutional sign-off and submission of completed applications. Remain current on federal and state laws, regulations, sponsor policies, and best practices relevant to sponsored projects. Manage grant records, including proposal submissions, pending applications, awards, declines, reporting requirements, and other relevant data. Advise the grants coordinator on the timely and appropriate expenditure of grant funds and on reporting requirements. Contribute to the development and implementation of institutional policies, procedures, and best practices related to sponsored projects and grant administration. Inform the work of the grants coordinator related to timely/appropriate expending of budget lines for grant projects and reporting. Work collaboratively with Advancement colleagues to identify prospective funders, coordinate institutional priorities, share relevant faculty and program information, and contribute to strategies for major solicitations. Participate in the development of collaborative and institutional proposals that draw on the expertise of faculty, academic programs, and administrative partners across the College. Qualifications Bachelor’s degree (Master’s/PhD preferred). At least 3-5 years of supervisory and institutional leadership over a pre-award or combined pre/post-award office. Minimum of 5 years of experience in grants administration, sponsored programs, research administration, or a related field, preferably in higher education or another complex institutional environment. Proven facility navigating online funding portals, (especially Research.gov , Grants.gov , commons.era.nih.gov , and Fastlane.NSF.gov ). Experience serving as an authorized organizational representative (AOR) for an institution of higher education. Record of successful support of competitive grant applications across a variety of disciplines (personally successful individual grant awardee preferred). Demonstrable experience editing and managing federal and other sponsored grants. Participation in development of institutional grants administration policies/procedures. Demonstrated collegiality and collaborative leadership, with highly developed communication, interpersonal skills, and the ability to build effective relationships across diverse constituencies. Application Process: Applicants should submit a cover letter, resume, and the names and contact information of references. Your cover letter should describe how your background, interests, and experience align with the position and how you plan to support Kenyon's work and mission. The position is open until filled. All inquiries can be sent to Travis Landry, Associate Provost, landryt@kenyon.edu . Compensation and Benefits Salaries at Kenyon are competitive and commensurate with experience. In addition to an attractive salary, Kenyon offers benefits for employees and their family members. Children of employees are eligible for 100% tuition waivers at Kenyon, and through the Great Lakes Colleges Association, children of employees are eligible for 90% tuition waivers at twenty-three other of the nation's finest liberal arts colleges. We also offer health, dental, and vision insurance, TIAA retirement, and many other benefits, including provisions for a spouse, families, and domestic partners. Details about benefits as well as conditions of employment are described more fully in our Staff Handbook. About Kenyon College Kenyon College is situated on a beautiful 1,200-acre hilltop campus in Gambier, a picturesque village in central Ohio. The College offers a quiet and intellectually stimulating environment approximately four miles from the city of Mount Vernon and within an hour’s drive of Columbus, a vibrant and growing city known for its thriving arts and cultural scene, diverse neighborhoods, excellent dining, and strong business and innovation communities. Kenyon College is an equal opportunity employer, and we welcome applications from all qualified individuals. It is the College's policy to evaluate qualified applicants without regard to race, color, national origin, ancestry, sex, gender, gender identity, gender expression, sexual orientation, physical and/or mental disability, age, religion, medical condition, veteran status, marital status, or any other characteristic protected by institutional policy or state, local, or federal law. Kenyon College has a strong commitment to an inclusive environment that welcomes all voices and perspectives. Back to job search Apply Now First Name (required) ebc489d9 Last Name (required) be53531e Email (required) 4b14585c Refer someone to this job Apply Please wait... Done Not You? Thank you Recommended Jobs Assistant Director of Student Engagement (11 month) Ohio Five Colleges, Ohio Student Engagement Kenyon College is conducting a search for a qualified candidate to fill the position of Assistant Director of Student Engagement. In cooperation with other Student Affairs staff members, the Assistant Director shares an awareness of and concern for all aspects of student academic, residential, and co-curricular life. In particular, the Assistant Director of Student Engagement will support the ongoing work of student organization finance management and will serve as the department’s advisor to the campus programming board. The Assistant Director of Student Engagement is an eleven (11) month reporting position. The work of the Assistant Director of Student Engagement includes regular evening and weekend responsibilities. Strategic Initiative Project Coordinator Gambier, OH, Ohio Office of the President Kenyon College is conducting a search for a qualified candidate to fill the position of Strategic Initiatives Project Coordinator in the Office of the President to support several of the college’s strategic initiatives, including Kenyon Keys, pre-college and destination programs, as well as academic and institutional partnerships, among others. Many of these programs are interdisciplinary and will cross traditional departmental boundaries, but they operate under the ultimate direction of the special assistant to the president for strategic initiatives and partnerships. The project coordinator will be an important partner for these programs, providing high-level logistical and administrative support, as well as occasional general support for the president’s division. This is a twelve-month position that will support logistics, maintain records, handle financial transactions, and support meetings and events. Notably, this position may serve as the on-site liaison for one or more of the Kenyon destination city programs, so some episodic summer travel may be required. This is a new position connected to the college's strategic initiatives; therefore, it will evolve over time as programs develop and change, and the project coordinator will have the opportunity to participate in that evolution. Senior Associate Director of Alumni Career Connections Gambier, OH, Ohio Alumni and Parent Engagement Kenyon College is conducting a search for a qualified candidate to fill the position of Senior Associate Director of Alumni Career Connections. The Senior Associate Director of Alumni Career Connections co-reports to the Director of Alumni Engagement and the Dean of the Career Development Office (CDO). This role will direct the mentorship and alumni connections unit within the CDO and be responsible for executing the overall volunteerism and mentorship strategy related to careers and experiential education. Sign up for job alerts First Name (required) 51c53c0d Last Name (required) 74aec9fd Email (required) d172d559 Job Alert c7b88bd1 Finalize your job alert by selecting criteria from the dropdowns below. You can select multiple options from each dropdown by returning to the combobox and re-entering the list of options. Submit at the end to create your job alert. Departments Provost Provost Employment Type Exempt Staff Exempt Staff Locations Gambier, OH, Ohio, United States Gambier, OH, Ohio, United States Send Please wait... Done Not You? Thank you Candidate Details We use cookies Some are necessary to operate the website and its functions. Others help personalise, improve content and services to show you the most relevant job opportunities. With the decision \"Accept essential only\" we will respect your privacy and will not set cookies that aren't necessary for the operation of the site. Accept essential only Accept all Please choose the location(s)"
