    "https://careers.kenyon.edu/jobs/strategic-initiative-project-coordinator-gambier-oh-ohio-united-states": {
      "title": "Strategic Initiative Project Coordinator",
      "description": "Strategic Initiative Project Coordinator - Gambier, OH, Ohio, United States Strategic Initiative Project Coordinator - Gambier, OH, Ohio, United States Kiosk mode Job Opportunities Strategic Initiative Project Coordinator 493364 Gambier, OH, Ohio Office of the President Exempt Staff Add to favorites View favorites Kenyon College is conducting a search for a qualified candidate to fill the position of Strategic Initiatives Project Coordinator in the Office of the President to support several of the college’s strategic initiatives, including Kenyon Keys, pre-college and destination programs, as well as academic and institutional partnerships, among others. Many of these programs are interdisciplinary and will cross traditional departmental boundaries, but they operate under the ultimate direction of the special assistant to the president for strategic initiatives and partnerships. The project coordinator will be an important partner for these programs, providing high-level logistical and administrative support, as well as occasional general support for the president’s division. This is a twelve-month position that will support logistics, maintain records, handle financial transactions, and support meetings and events. Notably, this position may serve as the on-site liaison for one or more of the Kenyon destination city programs, so some episodic summer travel may be required. This is a new position connected to the college's strategic initiatives; therefore, it will evolve over time as programs develop and change, and the project coordinator will have the opportunity to participate in that evolution. Essential Functions Kenyon Keys Kenyon Keys is an interdisciplinary thematic program that advances curricular and co-curricular projects across divisions and departments of the college and helps students curate a portfolio of experiences, from internships to research to service to study abroad. For Kenyon Keys, the project coordinator may: Organize, manage, administer, and track applications and funding for internal funding opportunities; Track data related to courses and other academic priorities related to Keys; Create and manage Kenyon Connect (KCon) platform to support student engagement; and Provide general support for the Director of Kenyon Keys. Pre-College and Destination City Programs Kenyon is building a series of immersive pre-college cohort programs for prospective high school juniors and seniors focused on a single area of study, designed to engage students on a specific topic and introduce them to a liberal arts education. Kenyon is also developing a series of intensive destination city programs for current Kenyon students who will engage deeply with a subject, learn from Kenyon faculty, explore topics with industry experts, and make important connections with Kenyon alumni and parent networks. For these initiatives, the project coordinator may: Collaborate with the director of experiential programming who manages pre-college summer programs and city programs for college students; Serve as on-site support for pre-college programs; and Serve as on-site liaison for destination. Academic and Institutional Partnerships Building on existing agreements with graduate and professional schools, Kenyon is developing new partnerships with key universities that facilitate pathways for current students to enter graduate programs and collaborate on educational opportunities. In addition, Kenyon is forging pathways for students to transfer from select Community Colleges into specific Kenyon programs. In supporting the special assistant for strategic initiatives and partnerships, the project coordinator may: Aid in planning visits and partnership-related events. Assist in promoting partnership programs by producing and disseminating information to various audiences General Administrative Duties Support planning and logistics for meetings and events of the strategic initiatives leadership team. Maintain records for semi-annual and year-end reporting. Organize the logistics for programs, partner relations, and speaker visits, including travel, ground transportation, accommodations, and room reservations. Process payment orders, reimbursements, Kenyon Commerce orders, and reconcile p-card statements. Maintain electronic files and records of all financial transactions connected to strategic initiatives and Kenyon Keys. Assist with the development of curricular connections and future notations for Kenyon Keys. Liaise with faculty and staff constituents across campus. Liaise with relevant departments regarding advertisement of events related to programming, including assisting with designing posters and adding events to BigTree and Top Desk, and the Kenyon calendar. Assist with updating Kenyon Keys and other strategic initiative web pages. Provide administrative and logistical support for the president’s division. e.g., ceremonies, building management, financial processing, etc., as requested. Knowledge, Skills, Abilities and Success Factors Detail-oriented in planning, written communication, and budgeting. Ability to establish priorities and use time wisely to accomplish tasks and assignments. Be highly motivated and very adaptable to change. Have outstanding organizational skills and event planning expertise. Be able to take initiative and be very productive. Be adept in Google and Microsoft Office (Word/mail merges, PowerPoint and Excel) and electronic file management. Be willing to learn new platforms, such as Kenyon Commerce, KCon, ASANA, or SLATE (as necessary). Be extremely dependable and able to work well as part of a team. Have excellent written and oral communication skills. Demonstrate superb attention to detail. This position requires travel to provide logistical support for various programs. Travel may comprise up to 20% of this position, as the Project Coordinator provides logistical support for off-site programs or partnerships. Minimum Qualifications Intellectual curiosity and interest in continuing to learn new things. Four-year college degree (preferred) or a combination of two-year degree and previous experience. Attention to detail. Organizational management experience. Ability to toggle between different tasks at different levels. Experience in planning meetings and/or organizing large projects. Ability to do independent long- and short-range planning. Willingness to work occasional weekends and evenings. Kenyon College is a nationally prominent, private liberal arts college where academic excellence goes hand in hand with a strong sense of community and close relationships among students and professors. Compensation and Benefits Salaries at Kenyon are competitive and commensurate with experience. In addition to an attractive salary, Kenyon offers benefits for employees and their family members. Children of employees are eligible for 100% tuition waivers at Kenyon, and through the Great Lakes Colleges Association , children of employees are eligible for 90% tuition waivers at twenty-three other of the nation's finest liberal arts colleges. We also offer health, dental and vision insurance, TIAA retirement, and many other benefits , including provisions for a spouse, families, and domestic partners. Details about benefits as well as conditions of employment are described more fully in our Staff Handbook . Kenyon is a unique place to live and work. To discover why it should be your next home, click here . Kenyon College is an equal opportunity employer, and we welcome applications from all qualified individuals. It is the College's policy to evaluate qualified applicants without regard to race, color, national origin, ancestry, sex, gender, gender identity, gender expression, sexual orientation, physical and/or mental disability, age, religion, medical condition, veteran status, marital status, or any other characteristic protected by institutional policy or state, local, or federal law. Kenyon College has a strong commitment to an inclusive environment that welcomes all voices and perspectives. Back to job search Apply Now First Name (required) 188343ed Last Name (required) 8f1708d8 Email (required) 45859871 Refer someone to this job Apply Please wait... Done Not You? Thank you Recommended Jobs Executive Assistant for The Kenyon Review Gambier, OH, Ohio Kenyon Review The Executive Assistant plays a central role in supporting the organization's leadership and ensuring smooth day-to-day operations by providing including grant coordination, gift acknowledgement, board administration, and conference/event logistics. The ideal candidate is highly organized, proactive, and passionate about supporting the literary arts. Assistant Director of Academic Advising for Fellowships and Scholarships Gambier, OH, Ohio Dean for Academic Advising The Assistant Director of Academic Advising for National Fellowships and Scholarships is a member of the Academic Advising team and reports to the Dean for Academic Advising and Support. This position provides leadership for Kenyon’s national fellowships and scholarships advising, including recruiting applicants, coordinating campus selection and review processes, supporting faculty involvement, and advising students as they prepare competitive applications. In addition to this primary focus, the Assistant Director supports the broader work of the Academic Advising Office. Responsibilities include assisting with faculty advising programs, monitoring student academic progress, supporting students facing academic challenges, and contributing to campus-wide initiatives that promote student success. Senior Associate Director of Alumni Career Connections Gambier, OH, Ohio Alumni and Parent Engagement Kenyon College is conducting a search for a qualified candidate to fill the position of Senior Associate Director of Alumni Career Connections. The Senior Associate Director of Alumni Career Connections co-reports to the Director of Alumni Engagement and the Dean of the Career Development Office (CDO). This role will direct the mentorship and alumni connections unit within the CDO and be responsible for executing the overall volunteerism and mentorship strategy related to careers and experiential education. Sign up for job alerts First Name (required) fbf07d8c Last Name (required) bac9ded0 Email (required) eff71ebf Job Alert 5b65d976 Finalize your job alert by selecting criteria from the dropdowns below. You can select multiple options from each dropdown by returning to the combobox and re-entering the list of options. Submit at the end to create your job alert. Departments Office of the President Office of the President Employment Type Exempt Staff Exempt Staff Locations Gambier, OH, Ohio, United States Gambier, OH, Ohio, United States Send Please wait... Done Not You? Thank you Candidate Details We use cookies Some are necessary to operate the website and its functions. Others help personalise, improve content and services to show you the most relevant job opportunities. With the decision \"Accept essential only\" we will respect your privacy and will not set cookies that aren't necessary for the operation of the site. Accept essential only Accept all Please choose the location(s)"
