    "https://careers.kenyon.edu/jobs/assistant-director-of-academic-advising-for-fellowships-and-scholarships-gambier-oh-ohio-united-states": {
      "title": "Assistant Director of Academic Advising for Fellowships and Scholarships",
      "description": "Assistant Director of Academic Advising for Fellowships and Scholarships - Gambier, OH, Ohio, United States Assistant Director of Academic Advising for Fellowships and Scholarships - Gambier, OH, Ohio, United States Kiosk mode Job Opportunities Assistant Director of Academic Advising for Fellowships and Scholarships 493365 Gambier, OH, Ohio Dean for Academic Advising Exempt Staff Add to favorites View favorites Kenyon College is conducting a search for a qualified candidate to fill the position of Assistant Director of Academic Advising for National Fellowships and Scholarships. The Assistant Director of Academic Advising for National Fellowships and Scholarships is a member of the Academic Advising team and reports to the Dean for Academic Advising and Support. This position provides leadership for Kenyon’s national fellowships and scholarships advising, including recruiting applicants, coordinating campus selection and review processes, supporting faculty involvement, and advising students as they prepare competitive applications. In addition to this primary focus, the Assistant Director supports the broader work of the Academic Advising Office. Responsibilities include assisting with faculty advising programs, monitoring student academic progress, supporting students facing academic challenges, and contributing to campus-wide initiatives that promote student success. Key Position Responsibilities National Fellowships and Scholarships The Assistant Director will coordinate and strengthen Kenyon’s national fellowships and scholarships program by: Recruiting and supporting student applicants for nationally competitive fellowships and scholarships. Organizing information sessions, workshops, and outreach efforts for individual scholarship and fellowship opportunities, including the annual Sophomore Scholarship reception with the President. Advising students who are exploring, preparing for, or applying to nationally competitive awards. Identifying and publicizing fellowship and scholarship opportunities that align with student interests and institutional strengths. Soliciting and coordinating faculty liaisons for national fellowships and scholarships. Convening meetings of the faculty Fellowships Committee. Coordinating feedback from faculty, committee, and campus partners on student applications. Publicizing student and alumni fellowship successes in collaboration with appropriate campus partners. Faculty Advising and Academic Advising Programs The Assistant Director will assist the Dean for Academic Advising and Support in supporting Kenyon’s faculty advising program by: Managing advisor reassignments related to faculty leaves, sabbaticals, and other staffing changes. Assisting with faculty advisor assignments, including the creation of advising teams. Helping plan and coordinate group advising meetings. Representing the Academic Advising Office at campus events such as Off-Campus Study Information Day, Sophomore Day, and other advising-related programs. Collaborating with the Center for Global Engagement, the Registrar’s Office, and other campus partners to support coordinated advising efforts. Advising students navigating the Academic Integrity Process, as directed by the Dean for Academic Advising and Support. Monitoring Student Academic Progress and Supporting Student Success The Assistant Director will help monitor academic progress and provide direct support to students by: Communicating with faculty about student academic performance, as directed by the Dean for Academic Advising and Support. Preparing reports on student academic progress for the Dean. Managing a caseload of students, including students on Conditional Enrollment, Kenyon’s academic probation program, and working to connect students to appropriate support resources on campus. Required Qualifications Bachelor’s degree required. Experience in academic advising, student success, fellowships advising, higher education administration, or a related field. Strong written and oral communication skills. Excellent organizational and project-management skills. Ability to work collaboratively with students, faculty, staff, and campus partners. Ability to manage confidential student information with discretion. Preferred Qualifications Master’s degree or advanced degree. Experience advising students on nationally competitive fellowships, scholarships, graduate study, or research opportunities. Familiarity with selective liberal arts college environments. Experience coordinating committees, application processes, or campus selection procedures. Knowledge of academic progress policies, academic probation processes, or student support systems. Kenyon College is a nationally prominent, private liberal arts college where academic excellence goes hand in hand with a strong sense of community and close relationships among students and professors. Compensation and Benefits Salaries at Kenyon are competitive and commensurate with experience. In addition to an attractive salary, Kenyon offers benefits for employees and their family members. Children of employees are eligible for 100% tuition waivers at Kenyon, and through the Great Lakes Colleges Association , children of employees are eligible for 90% tuition waivers at twenty-three other of the nation's finest liberal arts colleges. We also offer health, dental and vision insurance, TIAA retirement, and many other benefits , including provisions for a spouse, families, and domestic partners. Details about benefits as well as conditions of employment are described more fully in our Staff Handbook . Kenyon is a unique place to live and work. To discover why it should be your next home, click here . Kenyon College is an equal opportunity employer, and we welcome applications from all qualified individuals. It is the College's policy to evaluate qualified applicants without regard to race, color, national origin, ancestry, sex, gender, gender identity, gender expression, sexual orientation, physical and/or mental disability, age, religion, medical condition, veteran status, marital status, or any other characteristic protected by institutional policy or state, local, or federal law. Kenyon College has a strong commitment to an inclusive environment that welcomes all voices and perspectives. Back to job search Apply Now First Name (required) 597f2047 Last Name (required) f675ee4d Email (required) 5058037f Refer someone to this job Apply Please wait... Done Not You? Thank you Recommended Jobs Strategic Initiative Project Coordinator Gambier, OH, Ohio Office of the President Kenyon College is conducting a search for a qualified candidate to fill the position of Strategic Initiatives Project Coordinator in the Office of the President to support several of the college’s strategic initiatives, including Kenyon Keys, pre-college and destination programs, as well as academic and institutional partnerships, among others. Many of these programs are interdisciplinary and will cross traditional departmental boundaries, but they operate under the ultimate direction of the special assistant to the president for strategic initiatives and partnerships. The project coordinator will be an important partner for these programs, providing high-level logistical and administrative support, as well as occasional general support for the president’s division. This is a twelve-month position that will support logistics, maintain records, handle financial transactions, and support meetings and events. Notably, this position may serve as the on-site liaison for one or more of the Kenyon destination city programs, so some episodic summer travel may be required. This is a new position connected to the college's strategic initiatives; therefore, it will evolve over time as programs develop and change, and the project coordinator will have the opportunity to participate in that evolution. Assistant Director of the First-Year Experience Gambier, OH, Ohio Dean of Students Kenyon College is conducting a search for a qualified candidate to fill the position of Assistant Director of the First Year Experience. The Assistant Director of the First-Year Experience will assist in the development, execution, and assessment of Orientation and First-Year Experience programming for new and transfer students. The Assistant Director works with partners across the College and draws upon national best practices and emerging trends in student transition, retention, and engagement. The Assistant Director will oversee Student and Family Summer Connection programming, assist in the coordination of Fall Orientation, and partner with the Director to build a comprehensive college-wide First-Year Experience Program. The Assistant Director will provide leadership for student staff selection and training, and developing a set of Orientation Engagement Community Opportunities. Assistant Director of Student Engagement (11 month) Ohio Five Colleges, Ohio Student Engagement Kenyon College is conducting a search for a qualified candidate to fill the position of Assistant Director of Student Engagement. In cooperation with other Student Affairs staff members, the Assistant Director shares an awareness of and concern for all aspects of student academic, residential, and co-curricular life. In particular, the Assistant Director of Student Engagement will support the ongoing work of student organization finance management and will serve as the department’s advisor to the campus programming board. The Assistant Director of Student Engagement is an eleven (11) month reporting position. The work of the Assistant Director of Student Engagement includes regular evening and weekend responsibilities. Sign up for job alerts First Name (required) 570a3514 Last Name (required) 58330fe7 Email (required) 6b1d01f8 Job Alert bde7fca9 Finalize your job alert by selecting criteria from the dropdowns below. You can select multiple options from each dropdown by returning to the combobox and re-entering the list of options. Submit at the end to create your job alert. Departments Dean for Academic Advising Dean for Academic Advising Employment Type Exempt Staff Exempt Staff Locations Gambier, OH, Ohio, United States Gambier, OH, Ohio, United States Send Please wait... Done Not You? Thank you Candidate Details We use cookies Some are necessary to operate the website and its functions. Others help personalise, improve content and services to show you the most relevant job opportunities. With the decision \"Accept essential only\" we will respect your privacy and will not set cookies that aren't necessary for the operation of the site. Accept essential only Accept all Please choose the location(s)"
