    "https://careers.kenyon.edu/jobs/student-accounts-coordinator-gambier-oh-ohio-united-states-ab2b8926-9706-4700-b293-bf5e176c60d2": {
      "title": "Student Accounts Coordinator",
      "description": "Student Accounts Coordinator - Gambier, OH, Ohio, United States Student Accounts Coordinator - Gambier, OH, Ohio, United States Kiosk mode Job Opportunities Student Accounts Coordinator 493351 Gambier, OH, Ohio Accounting Non-Exempt Staff Add to favorites View favorites Kenyon College is conducting a search for a qualified candidate to serve in the position of Student Accounts Coordinator for the Accounting Office. The hourly rate of pay for this full-time, with benefits, position is $17.96. Successful completion of duties requires a thorough understanding of, and adherence to, College Policies. Willingness and ability to work collaboratively as well as independently is required. General responsibility includes assistance in the management and maintenance of student account records, billings, receipts, maintenance of department records on Federal Perkins and Institutional student loans. Duties of this position include, but are not limited to the following: Communication with students, parents, student loan borrowers and responsible parties. Posting of miscellaneous charges, student payments, and receipts. Reconciliation of general ledger accounts and running the monthly billing process. Maintaining student loan records and processing payments. The candidate must be punctual, reliable and possess the ability to work with interruptions during periods of peak activity. Effective and professional communication skills are critical, as well as a high degree of organization and time management. Skilled use of Microsoft Word and Excel is required. Experience in an accounting or finance office and an Associate degree in accounting is preferred. Benefits Kenyon offers benefits for employees and their family members. Children of employees are eligible for 100% tuition waivers at Kenyon, and through the Great Lakes Colleges Association , children of employees are eligible for 90% tuition waivers at twenty-three other of the nation's finest liberal arts colleges. We also offer health, dental and vision insurance, TIAA retirement, and many other benefits , including provisions for a spouse, families, and domestic partners. Details about benefits as well as conditions of employment are described more fully in our Staff Handbook . Kenyon is a unique place to live and work. To discover why it should be your next home, click here . Kenyon College is an equal opportunity employer, and we welcome applications from all qualified individuals. It is the College's policy to evaluate qualified applicants without regard to race, color, national origin, ancestry, sex, gender, gender identity, gender expression, sexual orientation, physical and/or mental disability, age, religion, medical condition, veteran status, marital status, or any other characteristic protected by institutional policy or state, local, or federal law. Kenyon College has a strong commitment to an inclusive environment that welcomes all voices and perspectives. Back to job search Apply Now First Name (required) 52277881 Last Name (required) ffeb6cad Email (required) c70e34f0 Refer someone to this job Apply Please wait... Done Not You? Thank you Recommended Jobs Executive Assistant for The Kenyon Review Gambier, OH, Ohio Kenyon Review The Executive Assistant plays a central role in supporting the organization's leadership and ensuring smooth day-to-day operations by providing including grant coordination, gift acknowledgement, board administration, and conference/event logistics. The ideal candidate is highly organized, proactive, and passionate about supporting the literary arts. Custodian, Third Shift Gambier, OH, Ohio Maintenance Kenyon College is conducting a search for a qualified applicant to fill the position of Custodian, Third Shift. Maintaining college buildings and facilities, keeping them free of hazard and presenting a neat, clean appearance. Must have the ability to work independently and as a member of a team. The hourly rate of pay for this full-time with benefits position is $25.70/hour and includes a 7% shift differential. Work days are Monday-Friday, 10:00 p.m. to 6:30 a.m., with a 30-minute unpaid lunch. Strategic Initiative Project Coordinator Gambier, OH, Ohio Office of the President Kenyon College is conducting a search for a qualified candidate to fill the position of Strategic Initiatives Project Coordinator in the Office of the President to support several of the college’s strategic initiatives, including Kenyon Keys, pre-college and destination programs, as well as academic and institutional partnerships, among others. Many of these programs are interdisciplinary and will cross traditional departmental boundaries, but they operate under the ultimate direction of the special assistant to the president for strategic initiatives and partnerships. The project coordinator will be an important partner for these programs, providing high-level logistical and administrative support, as well as occasional general support for the president’s division. This is a twelve-month position that will support logistics, maintain records, handle financial transactions, and support meetings and events. Notably, this position may serve as the on-site liaison for one or more of the Kenyon destination city programs, so some episodic summer travel may be required. This is a new position connected to the college's strategic initiatives; therefore, it will evolve over time as programs develop and change, and the project coordinator will have the opportunity to participate in that evolution. Sign up for job alerts First Name (required) 34eea920 Last Name (required) 70651ffc Email (required) 02119f10 Job Alert 6eb7e704 Finalize your job alert by selecting criteria from the dropdowns below. You can select multiple options from each dropdown by returning to the combobox and re-entering the list of options. Submit at the end to create your job alert. Departments Accounting Accounting Employment Type Non-Exempt Staff Non-Exempt St