    "https://careers.kenyon.edu/jobs/assistant-professor-of-political-science-tenure-track-gambier-oh-ohio-united-states": {
      "title": "Assistant Professor of Political Science, tenure-track",
      "description": "Assistant Professor of Political Science, tenure-track - Gambier, OH, Ohio, United States Assistant Professor of Political Science, tenure-track - Gambier, OH, Ohio, United States Kiosk mode Job Opportunities Assistant Professor of Political Science, tenure-track 493349 Gambier, OH, Ohio Political Science Faculty Add to favorites View favorites The Department of Political Science at Kenyon College invites applications for a tenure-track position in Modern Political Theory. We seek an individual broadly trained in the history of political philosophy who would teach introductory and intermediate courses in political theory (Quest for Justice, Modern Quest), as well as advanced courses in their areas of speciality. Successful candidates will demonstrate a commitment to the liberal arts, strong teaching, deep understanding of the history surrounding political thought, and scholarly promise. All application materials must be submitted electronically to http://careers.kenyon.edu . A complete application will include: 1) a cover letter discussing the applicant’s education, teaching experience, and scholarly interests; 2) a curriculum vitae; 3) a statement of teaching philosophy; 4) a writing sample; 5) an unofficial graduate transcript; and 6) contact information for three references. Review of completed applications will begin immediately and will continue until the position is filled. To ensure full consideration, please submit all application materials by September 15, 2026. Additional materials may be requested from candidates at a later date. Kenyon College is a nationally prominent, private liberal arts college where academic excellence goes hand in hand with a strong sense of community and close relationships among students and professors. Compensation and Benefits Salaries at Kenyon are competitive and are commensurate with experience. There are a number of faculty development opportunities (e.g. travel, research funds, etc.) for which appointees are eligible. In addition to an attractive salary, Kenyon offers benefits for employees and their family members. Children of employees are eligible for 100% tuition waivers at Kenyon, and through the Great Lakes Colleges Association , children of employees are eligible for 85% tuition waivers at fifteen other of the nation's finest liberal arts colleges. We also offer health and dental insurance, TIAA retirement, and many other benefits, including provisions for a spouse, families, and domestic partners. Details about benefits as well as conditions of employment are described more fully in our Faculty Handbook . Kenyon is a great place to live and work. To discover why it should be your next home, click here . Kenyon College is an equal opportunity employer, and we welcome applications from all qualified individuals. It is the College's policy to evaluate qualified applicants without regard to race, color, national origin, ancestry, sex, gender, gender identity, gender expression, sexual orientation, physical and/or mental disability, age, religion, medical condition, veteran status, marital status, or any other characteristic protected by institutional policy or state, local, or federal law. Kenyon College has a strong commitment to an inclusive environment that welcomes all voices and perspectives. Back to job search Apply Now First Name (required) 2b5dcb22 Last Name (required) 3f8492be Email (required) f9cbbbdd Refer someone to this job Apply Please wait... Done Not You? Thank you Recommended Jobs Assistant Professor of Political Science & Environmental Studies Gambier, OH, Ohio Political Science The Political Science Department and Environmental Studies Department at Kenyon College invite applications for a tenure-track position beginning July 1, 2027. Qualified applicants will have a strong teaching and research background in comparative politics, environmental politics, and international relations. The successful candidate would be appointed in both Political Science (60%) and Environmental Studies (40%), teach established courses in the curricula of both departments, and contribute upper-level courses on environmental politics and policy in their areas of expertise. We will prioritize candidates with a strong record of teaching and research; a commitment to student advising and mentorship; and plans to incorporate student researchers into their research. All application materials must be submitted electronically to http://careers.kenyon.edu. A complete application will include: 1) a cover letter discussing the applicant’s teaching experience, research interests and scholarship; 2) a curriculum vitae; 3) a statement of teaching philosophy with evidence of teaching excellence and a discussion of courses that the candidate has taught and can teach; 4) a writing sample; 5) an unofficial graduate transcript; and 6) contact information for three references. Review of completed applications will begin immediately and will continue until the position is filled. To ensure full consideration, please submit all application materials by September 15, 2026. Additional materials may be requested from candidates at a later date. Assistant Professor of Environmental Studies and Biology, Tenure-track Gambier, OH, Ohio Biology Kenyon College invites applications for a tenure-track position in the Departments of Environmental Studies and Biology (Freshwater Ecosystem or Landscape Ecology) starting July 2027. We seek a broadly trained ecologist with expertise in freshwater ecosystem or landscape ecology whose research focuses on regional or global ecological or biogeochemical processes. Teaching expectations are 3 courses in the Environmental Studies Department and 2 courses in the Biology Department each year. We will prioritize candidates with a strong record of teaching and research, a commitment to student advising and mentorship, and plans to incorporate undergraduate students in their research. To apply, please visit http://careers.kenyon.edu. Assistant Professor of Statistics Gambier, OH, Ohio Mathematics Kenyon College seeks to fill a tenure-track position at the assistant professor level in the Department of Mathematics and Statistics beginning July 2027. A Ph.D. in statistics is required, as well as prior teaching experience, preferably at a U.S. college or university or an equivalent institution. Scholars in all areas of statistics are encouraged to apply. Successful candidates will be teacher scholars who have experience using active learning pedagogies and who maintain a strong research program. The ability and willingness to include undergraduates in research is also desirable. Applications should be submitted by September 21, 2026, to ensure full consideration. Begin the application process by registering and completing the demographic section of the Kenyon College application at http://careers.kenyon.edu/. All other materials must be submitted electronically via https://www.mathjobs.org/jobs/list/28634. Sign up for job alerts First Name (required) 961a2107 Last Name (required) 5352a20a Email (required) b89edb37 Job Alert 9b1ceb98 Finalize your job alert by selecting criteria from the dropdowns below. You can select multiple options from each dropdown by returning to the combobox and re-entering the list of options. Submit at the end to create your job alert. Departments Political Science Political Science Employment Type Faculty Faculty Locations Gambier, OH, Ohio, United States Gambier, OH, Ohio, United States Send Please wait... Done Not You? Thank you Candidate Details We use cookies Some are necessary to operate the website and its functions. Others help personalise, improve content and services to show you the most relevant job opportunities. With the decision \"Accept essential only\" we will respect your privacy and will not set cookies that aren't necessary for the operation of the site. Accept essential only Accept all Please choose the location(s)"
    },
    "https://careers.kenyon.edu/jobs/assistant-professor-of-statistics-gambier-oh-ohio-united-states-dee20ca2-8165-4303-98f4-72d8955eb95b": {
      "title": "Assistant Professor of Statistics",
      "description": "Assistant Professor of Statistics - Gambier, OH, Ohio, United States Assistant Professor of Statistics - Gambier, OH, Ohio, United States Kiosk mode Job Opportunities Assistant Professor of Statistics 493348 Gambier, OH, Ohio Mathematics Faculty Add to favorites View favorites Kenyon College seeks to fill a tenure-track position at the assistant professor level in the Department of Mathematics and Statistics beginning July 2027. A Ph.D. in statistics is required, as well as prior teaching experience, preferably at a U.S. college or university or an equivalent institution. Scholars in all areas of statistics are encouraged to apply. Kenyon faculty members are excellent teachers who maintain strong research programs. The successful applicant will expand and enhance the statistics course offerings of the department. Our department has a strong commitment to student-centered learning; thus, we are particularly interested in candidates with experience in active learning pedagogies. Ability and willingness to include undergraduates in research is also desirable. Kenyon College is a fully residential liberal arts institution, located in central Ohio with 1700 excellent undergraduate students and an outstanding reputation for teaching and scholarship. The department offers a major in mathematics with areas of emphasis in statistics, classical mathematics, and applied mathematics. We have nine full-time tenure-track faculty members teaching a full range of undergraduate mathematics and statistics courses, and we also contribute to an interdisciplinary concentration in computing. The typical teaching load is five courses per year. Kenyon offers competitive salaries and a generous benefits package for employees and their family members. All Kenyon faculty have funds available to support travel and faculty development. In addition, startup funds will be available, depending on the research needs of the individual. Applications should be submitted by September 21, 2026, to ensure full consideration. We will, however, continue to accept applications until the position is filled. Begin the application process by registering and completing the demographic section of the Kenyon College application at http://careers.kenyon.edu/.. All other materials must be submitted electronically via https://www.mathjobs.org/jobs/list/28634 . A complete application will consist of: 1. Cover letter describing interest in the open position; 2. Statement reflecting on the applicant's teaching and learning experiences, including experiences with and plans for teaching a diverse student population with inclusive pedagogy; 3. Statement describing the applicant's research accomplishments and future research directions; 4. Curriculum Vitae; 5. Unofficial Undergraduate Transcript; 6. Unofficial Graduate Transcript; 7. Three (3) letters of recommendation (at least one of which should address teaching). PLEASE NOTE: In order for your application packet to be considered complete, the demographic section of the Kenyon College application must be filled out, AND all application materials must be submitted electronically through the mathjobs.org website. Compensation and Benefits Salaries at Kenyon are competitive and are commensurate with experience. There are a number of faculty development opportunities (e.g. travel, research funds, etc.) for which appointees are eligible. In addition to an attractive salary, Kenyon offers benefits for employees and their family members. Children of employees are eligible for 100% tuition waivers at Kenyon, and through the Great Lakes Colleges Association , children of employees are eligible for 85% tuition waivers at fifteen other of the nation's finest liberal arts colleges. We also offer health and dental insurance, TIAA retirement, and many other benefits, including provisions for a spouse, families, and domestic partners. Details about benefits as well as conditions of employment are described more fully in our Faculty Handbook . Kenyon is a great place to live and work. To discover why it should be your next home, click here . Kenyon College is an equal opportunity employer, and we welcome applications from all qualified individuals. It is the College's policy to evaluate qualified applicants without regard to race, color, national origin, ancestry, sex, gender, gender identity, gender expression, sexual orientation, physical and/or mental disability, age, religion, medical condition, veteran status, marital status, or any other characteristic protected by institutional policy or state, local, or federal law. Kenyon College has a strong commitment to an inclusive environment that welcomes all voices and perspectives. Back to job search Apply Now First Name (required) 8bdf36a1 Last Name (required) 7a13bee7 Email (required) 81c37a94 Refer someone to this job Apply Please wait... Done Not You? Thank you Recommended Jobs Data Analytics Fellow for Advancement Gambier, OH, Ohio Advancement Information Svcs Kenyon College is seeking qualified applicants to fill the position of Data Analytics Fellow in the Advancement division. This position reports to the Director of Advancement Systems and will collaborate extensively with other members of the Advancement division. The Data Analytics Fellow’s primary focus is enhancing data comprehension, visibility, and usefulness through modeling, analyzing and presenting results to support strong decisions. This is an entry-level, two-year, full-time position that is eligible for benefits. It is designed as a postbaccalaureate position geared toward recent college graduates who want to gain experience and benefit from strong technical and professional mentorship. This is a hybrid position requiring three days on premises per week. Assistant Professor of Political Science & Environmental Studies Gambier, OH, Ohio Political Science The Political Science Department and Environmental Studies Department at Kenyon College invite applications for a tenure-track position beginning July 1, 2027. Qualified applicants will have a strong teaching and research background in comparative politics, environmental politics, and international relations. The successful candidate would be appointed in both Political Science (60%) and Environmental Studies (40%), teach established courses in the curricula of both departments, and contribute upper-level courses on environmental politics and policy in their areas of expertise. We will prioritize candidates with a strong record of teaching and research; a commitment to student advising and mentorship; and plans to incorporate student researchers into their research. All application materials must be submitted electronically to http://careers.kenyon.edu. A complete application will include: 1) a cover letter discussing the applicant’s teaching experience, research interests and scholarship; 2) a curriculum vitae; 3) a statement of teaching philosophy with evidence of teaching excellence and a discussion of courses that the candidate has taught and can teach; 4) a writing sample; 5) an unofficial graduate transcript; and 6) contact information for three references. Review of completed applications will begin immediately and will continue until the position is filled. To ensure full consideration, please submit all application materials by September 15, 2026. Additional materials may be requested from candidates at a later date. Assistant Professor of Environmental Studies and Biology, Tenure-track Gambier, OH, Ohio Biology Kenyon College invites applications for a tenure-track position in the Departments of Environmental Studies and Biology (Freshwater Ecosystem or Landscape Ecology) starting July 2027. We seek a broadly trained ecologist with expertise in freshwater ecosystem or landscape ecology whose research focuses on regional or global ecological or biogeochemical processes. Teaching expectations are 3 courses in the Environmental Studies Department and 2 courses in the Biology Department each year. We will prioritize candidates with a strong record of teaching and research, a commitment to student advising and mentorship, and plans to incorporate undergraduate students in their research. To apply, please visit http://careers.kenyon.edu. Sign up for job alerts First Name (required) ac43f5e9 Last Name (required) 32229f51 Email (required) 2d732c35 Job Alert 053022b2 Finalize your job alert by selecting criteria from the dropdowns below. You can select multiple options from each dropdown by returning to the combobox and re-entering the list of options. Submit at the end to create your job alert. Departments Mathematics Mathematics Employment Type Faculty Faculty Locations Gambier, OH, Ohio, United States Gambier, OH, Ohio, United States Send Please wait... Done Not You? Thank you Candidate Details We use cookies Some are necessary to operate the website and its functions. Others help personalise, improve content and services to show you the most relevant job opportunities. With the decision \"Accept essential only\" we will respect your privacy and will not set cookies that aren't necessary for the operation of the site. Accept essential only Accept all Please choose the location(s)"
