    "https://careers.kenyon.edu/jobs/assistant-professor-of-environmental-studies-and-biology-tenure-track-gambier-oh-ohio-united-states": {
      "title": "Assistant Professor of Environmental Studies and Biology, Tenure-track",
      "description": "Assistant Professor of Environmental Studies and Biology, Tenure-track - Gambier, OH, Ohio, United States Assistant Professor of Environmental Studies and Biology, Tenure-track - Gambier, OH, Ohio, United States Kiosk mode Job Opportunities Assistant Professor of Environmental Studies and Biology, Tenure-track 493346 Gambier, OH, Ohio Biology Faculty Add to favorites View favorites Kenyon College invites applications for a tenure-track position in the Departments of Environmental Studies and Biology (Freshwater Ecosystem or Landscape Ecology) starting in July 2027. We seek a broadly trained ecologist with expertise in freshwater ecosystem or landscape ecology, with an interest in contributing to an interdisciplinary department. To complement current faculty expertise, we seek candidates whose research focuses on regional or global ecological or biogeochemical processes, preferably in freshwater systems. Applicants should demonstrate a commitment to excellent teaching, including strong academic support, inclusive course experiences, and effective mentoring for our diverse student population. Teaching expectations are 5 courses per year, with 3 courses in the Environmental Studies Department (e.g., Introduction to Environmental Studies, Senior Seminar in Environmental Studies, and new lecture and/or lab courses at the upper level) and 2 courses in the Biology Department (e.g., Introductory Biology lecture or lab, Aquatic Systems Biology). Additional opportunities exist for interdisciplinary teaching and scholarship within and outside the sciences, including in Kenyon's interdisciplinary Program in Computing and the college's Science and Nature Writing initiative. We expect a vigorous research program that involves undergraduate students, leads to publications, and has potential to attract extramural funding. Applicants should hold a Ph.D degree; post-doctoral experience is preferred. We encourage applications from all groups historically underrepresented in the sciences. A complete application will be composed of 1) a cover letter (maximum 2 pages); 2) a Curriculum Vitae (no page limit); 3) a statement of the applicant's teaching philosophy that addresses the applicant’s experiences and plans for teaching a diverse student body (maximum 2 pages); 4) a statement of the applicant’s research and scholarship that includes plans for collaborative research with undergraduates (maximum 3 pages); 5) an unofficial graduate transcript; and 6) contact information for three professional references. All application materials must be submitted electronically through Kenyon's employment website: http://careers.kenyon.edu . Review of applications will begin on August 31, 2026. Please direct questions to Natalie Wright, Search Committee Chair ( wright1@kenyon.edu ). Kenyon College is a nationally prominent, private liberal arts college where academic excellence goes hand in hand with a strong sense of community and close relationships among students and professors. Situated along the beautiful Kokosing River, with a 700-acre nature preserve , Kenyon is an ideal place to study and teach ecology. Kenyon has an established record of preparing students for graduate study and research careers, ranking 8th nationally in the proportion of STEM graduates who go on to earn doctoral degrees. Our students regularly earn nationally competitive awards, including Fulbright Fellowships and National Science Foundation Graduate Research Fellowship Program awards. Compensation and Benefits Salaries at Kenyon are competitive and are commensurate with experience. There are a number of faculty development opportunities (e.g. travel, research funds, etc.) for which appointees are eligible. In addition to an attractive salary, Kenyon offers benefits for employees and their family members. Children of employees are eligible for 100% tuition waivers at Kenyon, and through the Great Lakes Colleges Association , children of employees are eligible for 85% tuition waivers at fifteen other of the nation's finest liberal arts colleges. We also offer health and dental insurance, TIAA retirement, and many other benefits, including provisions for a spouse, families, and domestic partners. Details about benefits as well as conditions of employment are described more fully in our Faculty Handbook . Kenyon is a great place to live and work. To discover why it should be your next home, click here . Kenyon College is an equal opportunity employer, and we welcome applications from all qualified individuals. It is the College's policy to evaluate qualified applicants without regard to race, color, national origin, ancestry, sex, gender, gender identity, gender expression, sexual orientation, physical and/or mental disability, age, religion, medical condition, veteran status, marital status, or any other characteristic protected by institutional policy or state, local, or federal law. Kenyon College has a strong commitment to an inclusive environment that welcomes all voices and perspectives. Back to job search Apply Now First Name (required) 76011532 Last Name (required) 98497c7c Email (required) b7003701 Refer someone to this job Apply Please wait... Done Not You? Thank you Recommended Jobs Assistant Professor of Biology (Molecular Biology), Tenure-track Gambier, OH, Ohio Biology The Biology Department at Kenyon College invites applications for a tenure-track position starting in July 2027. We seek a broadly trained molecular biologist with a demonstrated commitment to excellence in undergraduate teaching and research. The successful candidate will teach 5 courses per year, including introductory biology, Molecular Biology, its associated laboratory course, and upper level courses in the candidate’s area of expertise. The successful candidate is expected to establish an active research program that engages undergraduate collaborators, leads to publications, and has the potential to attract extramural funding. To apply, please visit http://careers.kenyon.edu. Assistant Professor of Political Science & Environmental Studies Gambier, OH, Ohio Political Science The Political Science Department and Environmental Studies Department at Kenyon College invite applications for a tenure-track position beginning July 1, 2027. Qualified applicants will have a strong teaching and research background in comparative politics, environmental politics, and international relations. The successful candidate would be appointed in both Political Science (60%) and Environmental Studies (40%), teach established courses in the curricula of both departments, and contribute upper-level courses on environmental politics and policy in their areas of expertise. We will prioritize candidates with a strong record of teaching and research; a commitment to student advising and mentorship; and plans to incorporate student researchers into their research. All application materials must be submitted electronically to http://careers.kenyon.edu. A complete application will include: 1) a cover letter discussing the applicant’s teaching experience, research interests and scholarship; 2) a curriculum vitae; 3) a statement of teaching philosophy with evidence of teaching excellence and a discussion of courses that the candidate has taught and can teach; 4) a writing sample; 5) an unofficial graduate transcript; and 6) contact information for three references. Review of completed applications will begin immediately and will continue until the position is filled. To ensure full consideration, please submit all application materials by September 15, 2026. Additional materials may be requested from candidates at a later date. Assistant Professor of Political Science, tenure-track Gambier, OH, Ohio Political Science The Department of Political Science at Kenyon College invites applications for a tenure-track position in Modern Political Theory. We seek an individual broadly trained in the history of political philosophy who would teach introductory and intermediate courses in political theory (Quest for Justice, Modern Quest), as well as advanced courses in their areas of specialty. Successful candidates will demonstrate a commitment to the liberal arts, strong teaching, deep understanding of the history surrounding political thought, and scholarly promise. To apply, please visit careers.kenyon.edu. Sign up for job alerts First Name (required) efcf00e3 Last Name (required) 6b26b894 Email (required) 48b6b450 Job Alert b9d164ec Finalize your job alert by selecting criteria from the dropdowns below. You can select multiple options from each dropdown by returning to the combobox and re-entering the list of options. Submit at the end to create your job alert. Departments Biology Biology Employment Type Faculty Faculty Locations Gambier, OH, Ohio, United States Gambier, OH, Ohio, United States Send Please wait... Done Not You? Thank you Candidate Details We use cookies Some are necessary to operate the website and its functions. Others help personalise, improve content and services to show you the most relevant job opportunities. With the decision \"Accept essential only\" we will respect your privacy and will not set cookies that aren't necessary for the operation of the site. Accept essential only Accept all Please choose the location(s)"
