      "description": "Assistant Professor of Biology (Molecular Biology), Tenure-track - Gambier, OH, Ohio, United States Assistant Professor of Biology (Molecular Biology), Tenure-track - Gambier, OH, Ohio, United States Kiosk mode Job Opportunities Assistant Professor of Biology (Molecular Biology), Tenure-track 493345 Gambier, OH, Ohio Biology Faculty Add to favorites View favorites Kenyon College invites applications for a tenure-track position in the Department of Biology starting in July 2027. We seek a broadly trained molecular biologist with a demonstrated commitment to excellence in undergraduate teaching and research. We welcome applicants working in any area of molecular biology, including but not limited to gene expression and regulation, genomics, structural biology, protein structure and function, and/or computational molecular biology. The successful candidate will join a collaborative department dedicated to outstanding teaching, close faculty-student mentoring, and active undergraduate research. The successful candidate will also contribute to Kenyon's interdisciplinary Biochemistry and Molecular Biology (BMB) program. We seek applicants who demonstrate a commitment to inclusive teaching practices, strong academic support for students, and effective mentoring for a diverse student population. Teaching expectations are 5 courses per year, including introductory biology, Molecular Biology, its associated laboratory course, and upper level courses in the candidate’s area of expertise. Opportunities exist for interdisciplinary teaching and scholarship within and beyond the natural sciences. The successful candidate is expected to establish an active research program that engages undergraduate collaborators, leads to publications, and has the potential to attract extramural funding. Applicants must hold a Ph.D. degree; post-doctoral experience is preferred. We encourage applications from all groups historically underrepresented in the sciences. A complete application will be composed of 1) a cover letter (maximum 2 pages); 2) a Curriculum Vitae (no page limit); 3) a statement of the applicant's teaching philosophy that addresses the applicant’s experiences and plans for teaching a diverse student body (maximum 2 pages); 4) a statement of the applicant’s research and scholarship that includes plans for collaborative research with undergraduates (maximum 3 pages); 5) an unofficial graduate transcript; and 6) contact information for three professional references. All application materials must be submitted electronically through Kenyon's employment website: http://careers.kenyon.edu . Review of applications will begin on August 30, 2026. Please direct questions to Rebecca Clements, Search Committee Chair (clements1@kenyon.edu). Kenyon College is a nationally prominent, private liberal arts college where academic excellence goes hand in hand with a strong sense of community and close relationships among students and professors. Compensation and Benefits Salaries at Kenyon are competitive and are commensurate with experience. There are a number of faculty development opportunities (e.g. travel, research funds, etc.) for which appointees are eligible. In addition to an attractive salary, Kenyon offers benefits for employees and their family members. Children of employees are eligible for 100% tuition waivers at Kenyon, and through the Great Lakes Colleges Association , children of employees are eligible for 85% tuition waivers at fifteen other of the nation's finest liberal arts colleges. We also offer health and dental insurance, TIAA retirement, and many other benefits, including provisions for a spouse, families, and domestic partners. Details about benefits as well as conditions of employment are described more fully in our Faculty Handbook . Kenyon is a great place to live and work. To discover why it should be your next home, click here . Kenyon College is an equal opportunity employer, and we welcome applications from all qualified individuals. It is the College's policy to evaluate qualified applicants without regard to race, color, national origin, ancestry, sex, gender, gender identity, gender expression, sexual orientation, physical and/or mental disability, age, religion, medical condition, veteran status, marital status, or any other characteristic protected by institutional policy or state, local, or federal law. Kenyon College has a strong commitment to an inclusive environment that welcomes all voices and perspectives. Back to job search Apply Now First Name (required) 525cbcab Last Name (required) 5f4f146d Email (required) 5141e8d9 Refer someone to this job Apply Please wait... Done Not You? Thank you Recommended Jobs Assistant Professor of Environmental Studies and Biology, Tenure-track Gambier, OH, Ohio Biology Kenyon College invites applications for a tenure-track position in the Departments of Environmental Studies and Biology (Freshwater Ecosystem or Landscape Ecology) starting July 2027. We seek a broadly trained ecologist with expertise in freshwater ecosystem or landscape ecology whose research focuses on regional or global ecological or biogeochemical processes. Teaching expectations are 3 courses in the Environmental Studies Department and 2 courses in the Biology Department each year. We will prioritize candidates with a strong record of teaching and research, a commitment to student advising and mentorship, and plans to incorporate undergraduate students in their research. To apply, please visit http://careers.kenyon.edu. Assistant Professor of Political Science, tenure-track Gambier, OH, Ohio Political Science The Department of Political Science at Kenyon College invites applications for a tenure-track position in Modern Political Theory. We seek an individual broadly trained in the history of political philosophy who would teach introductory and intermediate courses in political theory (Quest for Justice, Modern Quest), as well as advanced courses in their areas of specialty. Successful candidates will demonstrate a commitment to the liberal arts, strong teaching, deep understanding of the history surrounding political thought, and scholarly promise. To apply, please visit careers.kenyon.edu. Assistant Professor of Statistics Gambier, OH, Ohio Mathematics Kenyon College seeks to fill a tenure-track position at the assistant professor level in the Department of Mathematics and Statistics beginning July 2027. A Ph.D. in statistics is required, as well as prior teaching experience, preferably at a U.S. college or university or an equivalent institution. Scholars in all areas of statistics are encouraged to apply. Successful candidates will be teacher scholars who have experience using active learning pedagogies and who maintain a strong research program. The ability and willingness to include undergraduates in research is also desirable. Applications should be submitted by September 21, 2026, to ensure full consideration. Begin the application process by registering and completing the demographic section of the Kenyon College application at http://careers.kenyon.edu/. All other materials must be submitted electronically via https://www.mathjobs.org/jobs/list/28634. Sign up for job alerts First Name (required) 8adf4905 Last Name (required) 834293fa Email (required) 752d4e8a Job Alert 79c32fe8 Finalize your job alert by selecting criteria from the dropdowns below. You can select multiple options from each dropdown by returning to the combobox and re-entering the list of options. Submit at the end to create your job alert. Departments Biology Biology Employment Type Faculty Faculty Locations Gambier, OH, Ohio, United States Gambier, OH, Ohio, United States Send Please wait... Done Not You? Thank you Candidate Details We use cookies Some are necessary to operate the website and its functions. Others help personalise, improve content and services to show you the most relevant job opportunities. With the decision \"Accep