    "https://careers.kenyon.edu/jobs/assistant-professor-of-political-science-environmental-studies-gambier-oh-ohio-united-states": {
      "title": "Assistant Professor of Political Science & Environmental Studies",
      "description": "Assistant Professor of Political Science & Environmental Studies - Gambier, OH, Ohio, United States Assistant Professor of Political Science & Environmental Studies - Gambier, OH, Ohio, United States Kiosk mode Job Opportunities Assistant Professor of Political Science & Environmental Studies 493344 Gambier, OH, Ohio Political Science Faculty Add to favorites View favorites The Departments of Political Science and Environmental Studies at Kenyon College, a highly selective, nationally-ranked liberal arts college in central Ohio, invite applications for a tenure-track position beginning July 1, 2027. Qualified applicants will have a strong teaching and research background in comparative politics, environmental politics, and international relations. The successful candidate would be appointed in both Political Science (60%) and Environmental Studies (40%), teach established courses in the curricula of both departments, and contribute upper-level courses on environmental politics and policy in their areas of expertise. The teaching load is five courses per year, three in Political Science and two in Environmental Studies. The search committee especially welcomes applications from candidates who could teach comparative politics courses for Political Science. Candidates should demonstrate their commitment to a career in the liberal arts. We will prioritize candidates with a strong record of teaching and research excellence; a commitment to student advising and mentorship; and plans to incorporate student researchers into their research programs. Candidates also must have a Ph.D. by the beginning of the appointment (July 2027). All application materials must be submitted electronically to http://careers.kenyon.edu . A complete application will include: 1) a cover letter discussing the applicant’s teaching experience, research interests and scholarship; 2) a curriculum vitae; 3) a statement of teaching philosophy with evidence of teaching excellence and a discussion of courses that the candidate has taught and can teach; 4) a writing sample; 5) an unofficial graduate transcript; and 6) contact information for three references. Review of completed applications will begin immediately and will continue until the position is filled. To ensure full consideration, please submit all application materials by September 15, 2026. Additional materials may be requested from candidates at a later date. Kenyon College is a nationally prominent, private liberal arts college where academic excellence goes hand in hand with a strong sense of community and close relationships among students and professors. If you have any questions, please email Victoria Grimaldo (grimaldo2@kenyon.edu) and/or search committee chair Jacqueline McAllister ( mcallisterj@kenyon.edu ). Compensation and Benefits Salaries at Kenyon are competitive and are commensurate with experience. There are a number of faculty development opportunities (e.g. travel, research funds, etc.) for which appointees are eligible. In addition to an attractive salary, Kenyon offers benefits for employees and their family members. Children of employees are eligible for 100% tuition waivers at Kenyon, and through the Great Lakes Colleges Association , children of employees are eligible for 85% tuition waivers at fifteen other of the nation's finest liberal arts colleges. We also offer health and dental insurance, TIAA retirement, and many other benefits, including provisions for a spouse, families, and domestic partners. Details about benefits as well as conditions of employment are described more fully in our Faculty Handbook . Kenyon is a great place to live and work. To discover why it should be your next home, click here . Kenyon College is an equal opportunity employer, and we welcome applications from all qualified individuals. It is the College's policy to evaluate qualified applicants without regard to race, color, national origin, ancestry, sex, gender, gender identity, gender expression, sexual orientation, physical and/or mental disability, age, religion, medical condition, veteran status, marital status, or any other characteristic protected by institutional policy or state, local, or federal law. Kenyon College has a strong commitment to an inclusive environment that welcomes all voices and perspectives. Back to job search Apply Now First Name (required) 56313cfa Last Name (required) f0fb47d2 Email (required) ff8073b9 Refer someone to this job Apply Please wait... Done Not You? Thank you Recommended Jobs Assistant Professor of Political Science, tenure-track Gambier, OH, Ohio Political Science The Department of Political Science at Kenyon College invites applications for a tenure-track position in Modern Political Theory. We seek an individual broadly trained in the history of political philosophy who would teach introductory and intermediate courses in political theory (Quest for Justice, Modern Quest), as well as advanced courses in their areas of specialty. Successful candidates will demonstrate a commitment to the liberal arts, strong teaching, deep understanding of the history surrounding political thought, and scholarly promise. To apply, please visit careers.kenyon.edu. Assistant Professor of Environmental Studies and Biology, Tenure-track Gambier, OH, Ohio Biology Kenyon College invites applications for a tenure-track position in the Departments of Environmental Studies and Biology (Freshwater Ecosystem or Landscape Ecology) starting July 2027. We seek a broadly trained ecologist with expertise in freshwater ecosystem or landscape ecology whose research focuses on regional or global ecological or biogeochemical processes. Teaching expectations are 3 courses in the Environmental Studies Department and 2 courses in the Biology Department each year. We will prioritize candidates with a strong record of teaching and research, a commitment to student advising and mentorship, and plans to incorporate undergraduate students in their research. To apply, please visit http://careers.kenyon.edu. Assistant Professor of Statistics Gambier, OH, Ohio Mathematics Kenyon College seeks to fill a tenure-track position at the assistant professor level in the Department of Mathematics and Statistics beginning July 2027. A Ph.D. in statistics is required, as well as prior teaching experience, preferably at a U.S. college or university or an equivalent institution. Scholars in all areas of statistics are encouraged to apply. Successful candidates will be teacher scholars who have experience using active learning pedagogies and who maintain a strong research program. The ability and willingness to include undergraduates in research is also desirable. Applications should be submitted by September 21, 2026, to ensure full consideration. Begin the application process by registering and completing the demographic section of the Kenyon College application at http://careers.kenyon.edu/. All other materials must be submitted electronically via https://www.mathjobs.org/jobs/list/28634. Sign up for job alerts First Name (required) b005f2fc Last Name (required) df395872 Email (required) 4192b9b2 Job Alert aaff6949 Finalize your job alert by selecting criteria from the dropdowns below. You can select multiple options from each dropdown by returning to the combobox and re-entering the list of options. Submit at the end to create your job alert. Departments Political Science Political Science Employment Type Faculty Faculty Locations Gambier, OH, Ohio, United States Gambier, OH, Ohio, United States Send Please wait... Done Not You? Thank you Candidate Details We use cookies Some are necessary to operate the website and its functions. Others help personalise, improve content and services to show you the most relevant job opportunities. With the decision \"Accept essential only\" we will respect your privacy and will not set cookies that aren't necessary for the operation of the site. Accept essential only Accept all