    "https://careers.kenyon.edu/jobs/assistant-professor-of-philosophy-gambier-oh-ohio-united-states": {
      "title": "Assistant Professor of Philosophy",
      "description": "Assistant Professor of Philosophy - Gambier, OH, Ohio, United States Assistant Professor of Philosophy - Gambier, OH, Ohio, United States Kiosk mode Job Opportunities Assistant Professor of Philosophy 493378 Gambier, OH, Ohio Philosophy Faculty Add to favorites View favorites The Philosophy Department of Kenyon College, a highly selective liberal arts college in central Ohio, invites applications for a tenure-track position in Ethical Theory, effective July 1st 2027. Qualified applicants must possess an AOS in Ethical Theory but should also possess broad philosophical interests. Though the AOC is open, candidates who can complement the current departmental strengths will be preferred. In particular, the philosophy department welcomes candidates with strength in one or more of the following: non-western philosophy, aesthetics, philosophy of language, philosophy of law. Teaching responsibilities consist of five courses per year. Candidates must have potential for high quality scholarship and a commitment to excellent teaching. Applicants must have a PhD in philosophy before the start of employment. The individual hired will be expected to teach courses ranging from Introductory-level philosophy courses to a Senior Level Ethics seminar. They will also be expected to engage actively in scholarship and participate in departmental and college service. Kenyon College is a fully residential liberal arts institution, located an hour northeast of Columbus, Ohio. We have 1700 excellent undergraduate students and an outstanding reputation for teaching and scholarship. The Philosophy Department at Kenyon is a congenial, pluralistic department, with broad interdisciplinary interests. Applications should be submitted by November 20, 2026, to ensure full consideration. We will, however, continue to accept applications until the position is filled. To apply, please visit http://careers.kenyon.edu . A complete application will include 1) a cover letter stating research interests and relevant professional background; 2) a curriculum vitae ; 3) a teaching portfolio that includes a teaching statement and at least one syllabus for a course in one’s specialty; 4) an unofficial transcript; and, if available, 5) evidence of teaching excellence. The Philosophy Department will solicit three letters of recommendation for each applicant who is closely considered. Kenyon College is a nationally prominent, private liberal arts college where academic excellence goes hand in hand with a strong sense of community and close relationships among students and professors. Compensation and Benefits Salaries at Kenyon are competitive and are commensurate with experience. There are a number of faculty development opportunities (e.g. travel, research funds, etc.) for which appointees are eligible. In addition to an attractive salary, Kenyon offers benefits for employees and their family members. Children of employees are eligible for 100% tuition waivers at Kenyon, and through the Great Lakes Colleges Association , children of employees are eligible for 85% tuition waivers at fifteen other of the nation's finest liberal arts colleges. We also offer health and dental insurance, TIAA retirement, and many other benefits, including provisions for a spouse, families, and domestic partners. Details about benefits as well as conditions of employment are described more fully in our Faculty Handbook . Kenyon is a great place to live and work. To discover why it should be your next home, click here . Kenyon College is an equal opportunity employer, and we welcome applications from all qualified individuals. It is the College's policy to evaluate qualified applicants without regard to race, color, national origin, ancestry, sex, gender, gender identity, gender expression, sexual orientation, physical and/or mental disability, age, religion, medical condition, veteran status, marital status, or any other characteristic protected by institutional policy or state, local, or federal law. Kenyon College has a strong commitment to an inclusive environment that welcomes all voices and perspectives. Back to job search Apply Now First Name (required) 75fcb799 Last Name (required) d255e4e4 Email (required) 70ec4a28 Refer someone to this job Apply Please wait... Done Not You? Thank you Recommended Jobs Marilyn Yarbrough Dissertation/Teaching Fellowship Gambier, OH, Ohio Provost This award is named in honor of the late Marilyn Yarbrough, Kenyon parent and trustee. A legal scholar and university administrator who was a former editor of the Black Law Journal and a member of the Pulitzer Prize Board, Marilyn Yarbrough often addressed gender and racial discrimination in her scholarship and teaching. In order to encourage such scholars to consider college rather than university teaching, Kenyon College offers the Marilyn Yarbrough Dissertation/Teaching Fellowship. The program is for scholars in the final stages of their doctoral work who need only to finish the dissertation to complete requirements for the Ph.D. We hope the experience of living and working for a year at Kenyon will encourage these fellows to consider a liberal arts college as a place to begin their careers as teachers and scholars. To apply, candidates should visit the online application site found at http://careers.kenyon.edu. A complete application will be composed of 1) a cover letter discussing the applicant’s research and scholarship undertaken, its relevance to the field or discipline, prior teaching experience, and the applicant's eligibility for the fellowship; 2) a Curriculum Vitae; and 3) contact information for three professional recommendations (system will automatically email reference writers). All application materials must be submitted electronically through Kenyon's employment website at http://careers.kenyon.edu The MYDF search will accept applications from mid-October through Dec. 31. Engagement Events Program Coordinator Gambier, OH, Ohio Alumni and Parent Engagement Kenyon College is searching for an Engagement Events Program Coordinator. Reporting to the Sr. Associate Director of Alumni and Parent Engagement Events, and will work closely with the Director of Alumni Engagement. The role will provide support for alumni, parent, and donor events sponsored by the Advancement Division and support to our campus partners as needed. Digital Stewardship Librarian Gambier, OH, Ohio Library Services Kenyon College is conducting a search for a qualified candidate to fill the position of Digital Stewardship Librarian. This 12 month, full time, position is primarily on campus with some remote flexibility. Help Kenyon's digital collections last. As our Digital Stewardship Librarian, you'll be the expert who makes sure our digitized and born-digital materials are preserved, findable, and put to good use by students, faculty, and researchers. What you'll do ● Administer Kenyon's repository platform and build workflows to describe, ingest, preserve, and migrate digital objects ● Advise on digital preservation, digitization, and asset management policy ● Lead digital projects and partner with faculty on grants, research, and course-integrated work ● Train and consult with faculty, students, and staff, including on information, digital, and AI literacy ● Serve as liaison to academic programs and represent Kenyon in OhioLINK and OH5 What you bring ● An ALA-accredited master's in library science (or equivalent) completed by June 2027, or a related degree plus library experience ● Education or experience in digital collections, digital preservation, metadata, or related work ● Strong communication skills and a knack for learning and teaching new technologies Interested in joining us? Apply through the Kenyon employment site with a cover letter, resume, and references. In your letter, we'd love to hear what draws you to this role, how your experience fits, and how you'd contribute to Kenyon's mission, along with your perspective on diversity, equity, inclusion, and accessibility. Applications are due by November 9, 2026. $58,000–$64,000 per year, commensurate with experience and qualifications. Sign up for job alerts First Name (required) 90b4b974 Last Name (required) 3b022308 Email (required) 01e66672 Job Alert fd256c45 Finalize your job alert by selecting criteria from the dropdowns below. You can select multiple options from each dropdown by returning to the combobox and re-entering the list of options. Submit at the end to create your job alert. Departments Philosophy Philosophy Employment Type Faculty Faculty Locations Gambier, OH, Ohio, United States Gambier, OH, Ohio, United States Send Please wait... Done Not You? Thank you Candidate Details We use cookies Some are necessary to operate the website and its functions. Others help personalise, improve content and services to show you the most relevant job opportunities. With the decision \"Accept essential only\" we will respect your privacy and will not set cookies that aren't necessary for the operation of the site. Accept essential only Accept all Please choose the location(s)"
